            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/docs/handoffs/triageflow-handoff-issue3.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Handoff — Issue #2 Complete → Issue #3 Ready\n2: \n3: **Session date:** 2026-05-29  \n4: **Session context:** `.tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue2-auth/context.md`  \n5: **Status:** All 6 subtasks complete, verified, pushed to all 3 repos.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## What Was Done (Issue #2 — User Authentication)\n10: \n11: Implemented JWT-based auth across Symfony backend and React frontend:\n12: \n13: | Repo | Remote | Head | Commits |\n14: |------|--------|------|---------|\n15: | Backend | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | `c46f04b` | 5 (test infra → entity → auth → test fix → key perms) |\n16: | Frontend | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | `9c09721` | 2 (scaffold → pages) |\n17: | Docs | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | `a7735fd` | 2 (raw_log → handoff) |\n18: \n19: ### Backend (19 tests, 46 assertions)\n20: - `User` entity: UUID PK, email (unique), roles (json), password (hashed), createdAt. `register()` named constructor, `promoteToAdmin()`.\n21: - `POST /api/register` — Symfony Validator constraints, duplicate-email 422, password hashing, JSON:API 201\n22: - `POST /api/login` — json_login firewall (already configured), returns JWT\n23: - `JWTSubscriber` — enriches JWT payload with `roles` claim on `lexik_jwt_authentication.on_jwt_created`\n24: - `services.yaml` — `UserRepository` → `DoctrineUserRepository` binding\n25: - `config/routes/user.yaml` — attribute-based routing for User controllers\n26: \n27: ### Frontend (tsc + eslint clean)\n28: - `useAuth` hook — JWT decode, login/logout, isAdmin from roles\n29: - `ProtectedRoute` + `AdminRoute` — React Router `<Navigate>` guards\n30: - `Header` — auth-aware nav (Login/Register vs authenticated links)\n31: - `AppLayout` — Header + Outlet\n32: - `LoginPage` — useMutation → POST /api/login → store JWT → redirect\n33: - `RegisterPage` — useMutation → POST /api/register → validation errors → redirect\n34: - `routes.tsx` — createBrowserRouter with all routes, lazy imports for admin\n35: - 6 stub pages for future issues (TriagePage, TriageResultPage, MySubmissionsPage, DashboardPage, SubmissionDetailPage, UsersPage)\n36: \n37: ---\n38: \n39: ## Current State\n40: \n41: ### Backend (Docker at `localhost:8000`)\n42: - 3 containers: `triageflow_php`, `triageflow_nginx`, `triageflow_db` (PostgreSQL 16)\n43: - Dev DB `triageflow` + test DB `triageflow_test` — both have `users` table from migration\n44: - `POST /api/register` + `POST /api/login` functional\n45: - JWT keys at `config/jwt/private.pem` + `config/jwt/public.pem`\n46: - DDD Light dirs exist: `src/{Triage,User,Admin,Shared}/`\n47: - Only User bounded context has code; Triage/Admin are empty dirs\n48: \n49: ### Frontend (Vite at `localhost:5173`)\n50: - `@tanstack/react-query` v5 + `react-router-dom` v7 configured\n51: - API client with JWT interceptor (Bearer + 401→/login redirect)\n52: - UI components: Button, Input, Card, Badge, Spinner, Loader, ErrorBoundary, EmptyState\n53: - All pages are stubs except LoginPage + RegisterPage (fully implemented)\n54: \n55: ### Packages Installed During Issue #2\n56: - `symfony/uid` — UUID generation (was missing from #1 scaffold)\n57: - `symfony/validator` — controller validation (was missing)\n58: - `symfony/browser-kit` — WebTestCase/KernelBrowser (was missing)\n59: - `phpunit/phpunit` v11 — test framework (was in composer.json but not installed)\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## Next: Issue #3 — Triage Pipeline\n64: \n65: Issue chain: #1→#2→**#3**→{#4, #5}→#6→#7 on `psswid/triageflow-docs`\n66: \n67: ### Reference Documents\n68: - **Backend plan**: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-28-backend-foundation.md` — Tasks 6, 9, 10, 11 (TriageSubmission entity, AI Analyzer, Submit command/handler, TriageController)\n69: - **Frontend plan**: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-28-frontend-foundation.md` — Tasks 4, 5, 6 (Triage interview, result page, submission list)\n70: - **Domain glossary**: `CONTEXT.md` — Triage Submission, Turn, Conversation History, Initial Symptom Description, Synthesis Case\n71: - **ADR 0002**: `docs/adr/0002-custom-ai-no-bundle.md` — No `symfony/ai-bundle`, AI via HTTP Client directly\n72: - **Coding standards**: `agents.md`, `backend/agents.md`\n73: \n74: ### What Issue #3 Needs\n75: \n76: **Backend** (from plan Tasks 6, 9, 10, 11):\n77: - TriageSubmission entity — UUID, User relation (ManyToOne), conversationHistory (json), status enum, specialist/urgency enums, isSynthetic, submittedAt/processedAt\n78: - TriageSubmissionRepository interface + Doctrine implementation\n79: - TriageSystemPrompt — medical triage prompt with specialist list + urgency + JSON output format\n80: - TriageAnalyzer — calls OpenRouter API via `symfony/http-client` (NOT symfony/ai — doesn't exist)\n81: - SubmitTriageCommand + SubmitTriageHandler — creates submission, dispatches async Message\n82: - ProcessTriageMessage — Messenger message for async AI processing\n83: - TriageController — POST /api/triage/submit, GET /api/triage/status/{id}, POST /api/triage/{id}/answer, GET /api/triage/result/{id}, GET /api/triage/submissions\n84: \n85: **Frontend** (from plan Tasks 4, 5, 6):\n86: - Replace TriagePage stub with symptom input form (textarea + submit)\n87: - Triage interview flow (poll for AI follow-up questions, display conversation, collect answers)\n88: - TriageResultPage — display specialist, urgency level (colored badge), justification, conversation history\n89: - MySubmissionsPage — list user's submissions with status badges, link to results\n90: \n91: ### Bootstrapping Notes\n92: - Backend Docker: `cd backend && docker compose up -d`\n93: - Backend commands inside Docker: `docker compose run --rm php composer ...` / `docker compose run --rm php bin/console ...`\n94: - Frontend: `cd frontend && npm run dev`\n95: - Backend tests: `docker compose run --rm php vendor/bin/phpunit`\n96: - Frontend checks: `npx tsc -b && npx eslint .`\n97: - Git: commit backend and frontend separately (different repos)\n98: - Test DB needs reset between runs: `docker compose run --rm php bin/console doctrine:database:drop --env=test --force --if-exists` then recreate+migrate\n99: - OpenRouter API key is in `backend/.env` as `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`\n100: \n101: ### Known Gaps / Watch Out For\n102: - **No DAMA bundle** — test DB is not transactionally isolated; use `uniqid()` for unique test data\n103: - **No symfony/ai-bundle** — doesn't exist on Packagist; use `symfony/http-client` directly with OpenRouter API\n104: - **UUID PK strategy** — use manual `Uuid::v4()` in constructor, not `doctrine.uuid_generator` (incompatible)\n105: - **No triage routes exist yet** — the auth test's `testProtectedEndpointRequiresAuth` uses GET /api/login returning 405; update to test real triage endpoint once TriageController exists\n106: - **Frontend stub pages need replacement** — TriagePage, TriageResultPage, MySubmissionsPage all render just a heading\n107: - **JWT private key permissions** — `private.pem` must be readable by `www-data` (PHP-FPM user in Docker). Fixed with `chmod 644` + Dockerfile RUN instruction at `c46f04b`. If login returns 500 \"Signature key does not exist\", check permissions inside container.\n108: \n109: ### Dependency Graph for Issue #3\n110: \n111: ```\n112: Task 6: TriageSubmission entity + repository + migration\n113:   ↓\n114: Task 9: TriageSystemPrompt + TriageAnalyzer service\n115:   ↓\n116: Task 10: SubmitTriageCommand + Handler + ProcessTriageMessage\n117:   ↓\n118: Task 11: TriageController (all 5 endpoints)\n119: ```\n120: \n121: Frontend (independent of backend, can run in parallel):\n122: ```\n123: Task 4: TriagePage (symptom input + interview flow)\n124: Task 5: TriageResultPage\n125: Task 6: MySubmissionsPage\n126: ```\n127: \n128: ---\n129: \n130: ## Suggested Skills\n131: \n132: | Skill | When |\n133: |-------|------|\n134: | `tdd-workflow` | Before writing ANY code — mandatory |\n135: | `b