            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/backend/agents.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # TriageFlow Backend — Agent Configuration\n2: \n3: > Symfony 7.4 API backend rules for AI agents. Load this file before ANY backend work (controllers, entities, AI integration, testing). Applies DDD Light architecture with bounded contexts: Triage, Admin, Reporting.\n4: \n5: ## Quick Reference\n6: \n7: ```bash\n8: # Create new Symfony project\n9: symfony new backend --version=\"7.4.*\" --webapp\n10: \n11: # Install core dependencies\n12: composer require symfony/ai-bundle symfony/scheduler symfony/messenger api\n13: composer require doctrine/orm doctrine/doctrine-migrations-bundle\n14: composer require lexik/jwt-authentication-bundle nelmio/cors-bundle\n15: composer require --dev phpunit/phpunit dama/doctrine-test-bundle phpstan/phpstan\n16: \n17: # Run tests\n18: php bin/phpunit\n19: \n20: # Run static analysis\n21: php vendor/bin/phpstan analyse\n22: \n23: # Generate migration\n24: php bin/console make:migration\n25: \n26: # Consume async queue (AI calls)\n27: php bin/console messenger:consume async\n28: \n29: # Consume scheduler (synthetic case generation)\n30: php bin/console messenger:consume scheduler_default\n31: ```\n32: \n33: ## Architecture: DDD Light with Bounded Contexts\n34: \n35: Inspired by `CodelyTV/php-ddd-example` and `mxkh/symfony-api-platform-ddd-cqrs-boilerplate`.\n36: \n37: ### Directory Structure per Context\n38: \n39: ```\n40: src/\n41: ├── Triage/                        # Bounded Context: Triage Pipeline\n42: │   ├── Application/\n43: │   │   ├── Command/\n44: │   │   │   ├── SubmitTriageCommand.php\n45: │   │   │   └── SubmitTriageHandler.php\n46: │   │   ├── Query/\n47: │   │   │   ├── GetTriageResultQuery.php\n48: │   │   │   └── GetTriageResultHandler.php\n49: │   │   └── Service/\n50: │   │       └── TriageAnalyzer.php       # AI analysis via symfony/ai Agent\n51: │   ├── Domain/\n52: │   │   ├── Entity/\n53: │   │   │   ├── TriageSubmission.php\n54: │   │   │   └── TriageResult.php\n55: │   │   ├── ValueObject/\n56: │   │   │   ├── Symptom.php\n57: │   │   │   ├── UrgencyLevel.php         # Enum: LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, EMERGENCY\n58: │   │   │   └── SpecialistType.php       # Enum: GP, CARDIOLOGIST, DERMATOLOGIST, etc.\n59: │   │   ├── Repository/\n60: │   │   │   └── TriageSubmissionRepository.php  # Interface only\n61: │   │   └── Event/\n62: │   │       └── TriageCompletedEvent.php\n63: │   └── Infrastructure/\n64: │       ├── Controller/\n65: │       │   └── TriageController.php     # Manual REST (shows senior patterns)\n66: │       ├── ApiResource/\n67: │       │   └── TriageSubmissionResource.php  # API Platform resource\n68: │       └── Repository/\n69: │           └── DoctrineTriageSubmissionRepository.php\n70: ├── Admin/                          # Bounded Context: Admin Panel\n71: │   ├── Application/\n72: │   ├── Domain/\n73: │   └── Infrastructure/\n74: │       ├── ApiResource/            # API Platform auto-CRUD\n75: │       │   └── AdminDashboardResource.php\n76: │       └── Controller/\n77: │           └── SyntheticCaseController.php  # Manual trigger\n78: └── Reporting/                      # Bounded Context: Statistics\n79:     ├── Application/\n80:     │   └── Query/\n81:     │       └── TriageStatsQuery.php\n82:     ├── Domain/\n83:     └── Infrastructure/\n84:         └── Controller/\n85:             └── StatsController.php\n86: ```\n87: \n88: ### Bounded Context Rules\n89: \n90: 1. **Each context has its own domain model** — no cross-context entity references\n91: 2. **Communication between contexts via Messenger events** — never via direct service calls\n92: 3. **Repository interfaces in Domain, implementations in Infrastructure**\n93: 4. **Value Objects for all domain primitives** — no stringly-typed code\n94: 5. **Read/Write separation** — Queries can bypass domain model; Commands always go through domain\n95: \n96: ## symfony/ai Integration\n97: \n98: ### Configuration (`config/packages/ai.yaml`)\n99: \n100: ```yaml\n101: ai:\n102:     platform:\n103:         generic:\n104:             deepseek:\n105:                 base_url: 'https://api.deepseek.com'\n106:                 api_key: '%env(DEEPSEEK_API_KEY)%'\n107:                 model_catalog: 'Symfony\\AI\\Platform\\Bridge\\ModelsDev\\ModelCatalog'\n108:     agent:\n109:         triage_agent:\n110:             platform: 'ai.platform.generic.deepseek'\n111:             model: 'deepseek-chat'\n112:             system_prompt: 'app.triage.system_prompt'\n113:             tools: false\n114:         triage_reasoner:\n115:             platform: 'ai.platform.generic.deepseek'\n116:             model: 'deepseek-reasoner'\n117:             system_prompt: 'app.triage.system_prompt'\n118:             tools: false\n119:         synthetic_agent:\n120:             platform: 'ai.platform.generic.deepseek'\n121:             model: 'deepseek-chat'\n122:             system_prompt: 'app.synthetic.system_prompt'\n123:             tools: false\n124: \n125: services:\n126:     Symfony\\AI\\Platform\\Bridge\\ModelsDev\\ModelCatalog:\n127:         arguments:\n128:             $providerId: 'deepseek'\n129: \n130:     app.triage.system_prompt:\n131:         class: Symfony\\Component\\DependencyInjection\\ParameterBag\\ParameterBag\n132:         # Defined in services.yaml as a parameter\n133: ```\n134: \n135: ### AI Integration Patterns\n136: \n137: ```php\n138: // ✅ CORRECT: TriageAnalyzer service using symfony/ai Agent\n139: declare(strict_types=1);\n140: \n141: namespace App\\Triage\\Application\\Service;\n142: \n143: use Symfony\\AI\\Platform\\PlatformInterface;\n144: use Symfony\\AI\\Platform\\Model\\Request;\n145: use Symfony\\AI\\Platform\\Model\\Response;\n146: \n147: final readonly class TriageAnalyzer\n148: {\n149:     public function __construct(\n150:         private PlatformInterface $aiPlatform,\n151:         private string $systemPrompt,\n152:     ) {}\n153: \n154:     public function analyze(array $symptoms, array $patientContext): TriageResultDto\n155:     {\n156:         $prompt = $this->buildPrompt($symptoms, $patientContext);\n157: \n158:         $response = $this->aiPlatform->request(new Request(\n159:             model: 'deepseek-chat',\n160:             messages: [\n161:                 ['role' => 'system', 'content' => $this->systemPrompt],\n162:                 ['role' => 'user', 'content' => $prompt],\n163:             ],\n164:             temperature: 0.3,  // Low temp for medical consistency\n165:             maxTokens: 1000,\n166:         ));\n167: \n168:         return TriageResultDto::fromAiResponse($response->content);\n169:     }\n170: \n171:     private function buildPrompt(array $symptoms, array $patientContext): string\n172:     {\n173:         // Structured prompt with medical context\n174:         return sprintf(\n175:             \"Patient symptoms: %s\\nContext: %s\\n\\nAnalyze and return JSON with: specialist, urgency, justification.\",\n176:             implode(', ', $symptoms),\n177:             json_encode($patientContext),\n178:         );\n179:     }\n180: }\n181: ```\n182: \n183: ### AI Call Rules\n184: \n185: 1. **Always use async** — AI calls go through Messenger transport (never blocking HTTP request)\n186: 2. **Always provide system prompt** — medical domain context + output format constraints\n187: 3. **Always validate AI output** — parse JSON, validate against enums, fallback on malformed\n188: 4. **Never expose raw AI output** — always transform through DTO before returning to client\n189: 5. **Retry on failure** — configure Messenger retry strategy for AI calls (max 3 attempts)\n190: 6. **Low temperature** (0.2-0.3) for medical analysis; higher (0.7) for synthetic data generation\n191: \n192: ### System Prompt Template\n193: \n194: ```\n195: You are a medical triage assistant. Analyze patient symptoms and provide:\n196: 1. Recommended specialist (one of: GP, CARDIOLOGIST, DERMATOLOGIST, NEUROLOGIST, ORTHOPEDIST, GASTROENTEROLOGIST, PULMONOLOGIST, PSYCHIATRIST)\n197: 2. Urgency level (one of: LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, EMERGENCY)\n198: 3. Brief medical justification (2-3 sentences)\n199: \n200: IMPORTANT: This is a DEMONSTRATION system. All data is synthetic. Never provide real medical advice.\n201: Respond ONLY with valid JSON: {\"specialist\": \"...\", \"urgency\": \"...\", \"justification\": \"...\"}\n202: ```\n203: \n204: ## Symfony 7.4 Conventions\n205: \n206: ### Code Style\n207: \n208: ```php\n209: // ✅ Correct\n210: declare(strict_types=1);\n211: \n212: namespace App\\Triage\\Domain\\Entity;\n213: \n214: use Doctrine\\ORM\\Mapping as ORM;\n215: \n216: #[ORM\\Entity]\n217: final class TriageSubmission\n218: {\n219:     public function __construct(\n220:         #[ORM\\Id, ORM\\GeneratedValue, ORM\\Column]\n221:         private readonly int $id,\n222: \n223:         #[ORM\\Column(type: 'json')]\n224:         private readonly array $symptoms,\n225: \n226:         #[ORM\\Embedded(class: UrgencyLevel::class)]\n227:         private readonly UrgencyLevel $urgency,\n228: \n229:         #[ORM\\Column]\n230:         private readonly \\DateTimeImmutable $submittedAt = new \\DateTimeImmutable(),\n231:     ) {}\n232: }\n233: ```\n234: \n235: ### Rules\n236: - **`declare(strict_types=1)`** in every PHP file\n237: - **`readonly` classes** for DTOs, Value Objects, Commands, Queries\n238: - **`final` classes** by default — open for extension only when designed\n239: - **Constructor property promotion** with `#[ORM\\]` attributes\n240: - **Named constructors** for domain objects: `TriageSubmission::create()`, `TriageSubmission::fromArray()`\n241: - **No setters** — immutable domain objects\n242: - **No inheritance** in entities — use composition (Embeddables)\n243: - **PHP 8.4 property hooks** where appropriate (getters without methods)\n244: \n245: ### Naming\n246: - **Controllers:** `{Resource}Controller` (TriageController, AdminController)\n247: - **Commands:** `{Action}{Resource}Command` (SubmitTriageCommand)\n248: - **Queries:** `Get{Resource}{Filter}Query` (GetTriageResultQuery)\n249: - **Handlers:** `{Command|Query}Handler` (SubmitTriageHandler)\n250: - **Entities:** Domain concepts as nouns (TriageSubmission, TriageResult)\n251: - **Value Objects:** Domain primitives (UrgencyLevel, SpecialistType, Symptom)\n252: - **Repositories:** `{Entity}Repository` interface in Domain, `Doctrine{Entity}Repository` in Infrastructure\n253: - **Events:** `{Entity}{Action}Event` (TriageCompletedEvent)\n254: \n255: ### Dependency Injection\n256: - **Constructor injection only** — never use `$container->get()` or service location\n257: - **Tagged iterators** for strategy patterns\n258: - **`autowire` + `autoconfigure`** — minimum manual service definitions\n259: - **Interface bindings** in `services.yaml`, never in entity constructors\n260: \n261: ## API Conventions\n262: \n263: ### REST API Design\n264: \n265: **Triage Pipeline (Manual Controllers):**\n266: ```\n267: POST   /api/triage/submit          # Submit symptom questionnaire\n268: GET    /api/triage/result/{id}     # Get AI triage result\n269: GET    /api/triage/status/{id}     # Check async processing status\n270: ```\n271: \n272: **Admin Panel (API Platform):**\n273: ```\n274: GET    /api/admin/submissions      # List all triaged submissions\n275: GET    /api/admin/submissions/{id} # View single submission\n276: PATCH  /api/admin/submissions/{id} # Update status/override\n277: GET    /api/admin/stats            # Dashboard statistics\n278: POST   /api/admin/synthetic/generate # Manually trigger synthetic case\n279: ```\n280: \n281: **Synthetic Data:**\n282: ```\n283: GET    /api/synthetic/status       # Generator health check\n284: ```\n285: \n286: ### Response Format\n287: \n288: All responses follow JSON:API-like conventions:\n289: \n290: ```json\n291: {\n292:   \"data\": {\n293:     \"id\": \"uuid\",\n294:     \"type\": \"triage_result\",\n295:     \"attributes\": {\n296:       \"specialist\": \"CARDIOLOGIST\",\n297:       \"urgency\": \"HIGH\",\n298:       \"justification\": \"Patient reports chest pain with radiating...\",\n299:       \"submittedAt\": \"2026-05-26T10:30:00+00:00\"\n300:     }\n301:   }\n302: }\n303: ```\n304: \n305: ### Error Responses\n306: \n307: ```json\n308: {\n309:   \"errors\": [{\n310:     \"status\": \"422\",\n311:     \"code\": \"VALIDATION_FAILED\",\n312:     \"title\": \"Validation Failed\",\n313:     \"detail\": \"Symptoms array must contain at least 1 item\"\n314:   }]\n315: }\n316: ```\n317: \n318: ### API Rules\n319: - **Async endpoints return 202** with status URL for polling\n320: - **Validation errors return 422** with specific field errors\n321: - **Auth errors return 401** (JWT expired) or 403 (insufficient permissions)\n322: - **Always return proper HTTP status codes** — never 200 for errors\n323: - **OpenAPI docs** auto-generated via API Platform (admin) + NelmioApiDoc (triage endpoints)\n324: \n325: ## Database & Doctrine\n326: \n327: ### Entities\n328: \n329: ```php\n330: #[ORM\\Entity]\n331: #[ORM\\Table(name: 'triage_submissions')]\n332: final class TriageSubmission\n333: {\n334:     #[ORM\\Id]\n335:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'uuid', unique: true)]\n336:     #[ORM\\GeneratedValue(strategy: 'CUSTOM')]\n337:     #[ORM\\CustomIdGenerator(class: UuidGenerator::class)]\n338:     private readonly Uuid $id;\n339: \n340:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'json')]\n341:     private readonly array $symptoms;\n342: \n343:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'string', enumType: UrgencyLevel::class)]\n344:     private readonly UrgencyLevel $urgency;\n345: \n346:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'string', enumType: SpecialistType::class)]\n347:     private readonly SpecialistType $recommendedSpecialist;\n348: \n349:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'text')]\n350:     private readonly string $aiJustification;\n351: \n352:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'json', nullable: true)]\n353:     private readonly ?array $aiRawResponse;\n354: \n355:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'string', length: 20)]\n356:     private readonly string $status; // pending, processing, completed, failed\n357: \n358:     #[ORM\\Column(type: 'boolean')]\n359:     private readonly bool $isSynthetic;\n360: \n361:     #[ORM\\Column]\n362:     private readonly \\DateTimeImmutable $submittedAt;\n363: \n364:     #[ORM\\Column(nullable: true)]\n365:     private readonly ?\\DateTimeImmutable $processedAt;\n366: }\n367: ```\n368: \n369: ### Database Rules\n370: - **UUID primary keys** — never auto-increment IDs in API-facing entities\n371: - **JSON columns** for AI responses, symptoms, flexible data\n372: - **PHP 8.4 Enums** mapped to Doctrine string columns\n373: - **`isSynthetic` flag** on all entities — easy filtering of AI-generated data\n374: - **Timestamps** — `submittedAt`, `processedAt` on every entity\n375: - **Migrations** — always generate via `make:migration`, review before committing\n376: - **No business logic in entities** — entities are data containers only\n377: \n378: ## Testing\n379: \n380: ### PHPUnit Configuration\n381: \n382: ```xml\n383: <!-- phpunit.xml.dist -->\n384: <phpunit>\n385:     <php>\n386:         <env name=\"KERNEL_CLASS\" value=\"App\\Kernel\" />\n387:         <env name=\"DATABASE_URL\" value=\"sqlite:///:memory:\" />\n388:         <env name=\"DEEPSEEK_API_KEY\" value=\"test_key\" />\n389:         <env name=\"APP_ENV\" value=\"test\" />\n390:     </php>\n391:     <extensions>\n392:         <extension class=\"DAMA\\DoctrineTestBundle\\PHPUnit\\PHPUnitExtension\"/>\n393:     </extensions>\n394: </phpunit>\n395: ```\n396: \n397: ### Test Patterns\n398: \n399: ```php\n400: // ✅ Unit test for TriageAnalyzer (with mocked AI)\n401: final class TriageAnalyzerTest extends KernelTestCase\n402: {\n403:     public function testAnalyzeReturnsValidResult(): void\n404:     {\n405:         $mockPlatform = $this->createMock(PlatformInterface::class);\n406:         $mockPlatform->method('request')\n407:             ->willReturn(new Response(content: json_encode([\n408:                 'specialist' => 'CARDIOLOGIST',\n409:                 'urgency' => 'HIGH',\n410:                 'justification' => 'Test justification',\n411:             ])));\n412: \n413:         $analyzer = new TriageAnalyzer(\n414:             aiPlatform: $mockPlatform,\n415:             systemPrompt: 'test prompt',\n416:         );\n417: \n418:         $result = $analyzer->analyze(\n419:             symptoms: ['chest pain'],\n420:             patientContext: ['age' => 45],\n421:         );\n422: \n423:         $this->assertSame(SpecialistType::CARDIOLOGIST, $result->specialist);\n424:         $this->assertSame(UrgencyLevel::HIGH, $result->urgency);\n425:     }\n426: \n427:     public function testAnalyzeHandlesMalformedAiResponse(): void\n428:     {\n429:         $mockPlatform = $this->createMock(PlatformInterface::class);\n430:         $mockPlatform->method('request')\n431:             ->willReturn(new Response(content: 'not json'));\n432: \n433:         $analyzer = new TriageAnalyzer($mockPlatform, 'test prompt');\n434: \n435:         $this->expectException(TriageAnalysisFailedException::class);\n436:         $analyzer->analyze(['symptom'], ['age' => 30]);\n437:     }\n438: }\n439: ```\n440: \n441: ### Testing Rules\n442: - **Unit tests for domain logic** — mock external dependencies (AI, DB)\n443: - **Integration tests for repositories** — use `DAMA\\DoctrineTestBundle` for isolated DB\n444: - **Functional tests for controllers** — test full request/response cycle\n445: - **Mock AI always** — never call real DeepSeek API in tests\n446: - **80%+ code coverage required** per OpenCode config\n447: - **Test error paths** — malformed AI responses, timeouts, invalid input\n448: - **Data providers** for validation edge cases\n449: \n450: ## Security\n451: \n452: - **JWT authentication** via `lexik/jwt-authentication-bundle`\n453: - **CORS configured** for frontend origin only\n454: - **Input validation** — Symfony Validator constraints on all DTOs\n455: - **No SQL injection** — Doctrine ORM + parameterized queries\n456: - **Rate limiting** on triage endpoint (prevent abuse)\n457: - **API keys in environment** — never committed, use `.env.local`\n458: - **HTTPS in production** — enforced via Symfony security config\n459: \n460: ## Scheduler: Synthetic Case Generator\n461: \n462: ```php\n463: // config/packages/scheduler.yaml\n464: framework:\n465:     scheduler:\n466:         synthetic_case_generation:\n467:             expression: '*/60 * * * *'  // Every 60 seconds\n468:             enabled: true\n469: ```\n470: \n471: ```php\n472: // Scheduled task handler\n473: #[AsCronTask('*/60 * * * *')]\n474: final class GenerateSyntheticCaseTask\n475: {\n476:     public function __construct(\n477:         private PlatformInterface $aiPlatform,\n478:         private EntityManagerInterface $em,\n479:     ) {}\n480: \n481:     public function __invoke(): void\n482:     {\n483:         $symptoms = $this->aiPlatform->request(new Request(\n484:             model: 'deepseek-chat',\n485:             messages: [[\n486:                 'role' => 'user',\n487:                 'content' => 'Generate 1 realistic but synthetic patient symptom set as JSON array of strings. Vary medical domains (cardiology, dermatology, neurology, etc).',\n488:             ]],\n489:             temperature: 0.7,\n490:         ));\n491: \n492:         // Create TriageSubmission with isSynthetic=true\n493:         // Dispatch to Messenger for processing\n494:     }\n495: }\n496: ```\n497: \n498: ## Related Files\n499: \n500: - `../agents.md` — Master project configuration\n501: - `../.opencode/config.json` — OpenCode configuration\n502: - `../.opencode/skills/triageflow/SKILL.md` — Domain conventions\n503: - `../frontend/agents.md` — Frontend rules\n504: - https://github.com/CodelyTV/php-ddd-example — Architecture inspiration\n505: - https://github.com/symfony/ai — symfony/ai package\n506: - https://symfony.com/doc/current/scheduler.html — Scheduler 