            "output": "<task id=\"ses_18b128b04ffe5ky6S9UGW8cmuw\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI now have a complete picture. Here is the comprehensive summary:\n\n---\n\n## Backend Codebase State — Comprehensive Summary\n\n### 1. Overall Architecture\n\nThe project uses **Symfony 7.4** with **DDD Light** (Domain-Driven Design, pragmatic version). The codebase is organized into **Bounded Contexts** (src/Triage/, src/User/, src/Admin/, src/Shared/), each with `Application/`, `Domain/`, and `Infrastructure/` subdirectories. The `agents.md` file outlines the full architecture specification — but the actual implementation is only partially complete.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Complete File Inventory\n\n#### 2a. `src/Triage/` (the target of Issue #3)\n\n| Directory | State |\n|-----------|-------|\n| `Application/` | **EMPTY** — no files |\n| `Domain/Entity/` | **EMPTY** — directory exists, no PHP files |\n| `Infrastructure/` | **EMPTY** — no files |\n\n**Verdict: Triage is a skeleton. Only the directory structure exists. Nothing is implemented.**\n\n#### 2b. `src/User/` (the reference implementation)\n\n| Path | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `Domain/Entity/User.php` | Full Doctrine entity with UUID, email, roles, password, createdAt |\n| `Domain/Repository/UserRepository.php` | Interface: `save()`, `findById()`, `findByEmail()` |\n| `Application/` | **EMPTY** — no command/query handlers yet |\n| `Infrastructure/Controller/AuthController.php` | Login endpoint (intercepted by firewall) |\n| `Infrastructure/Controller/RegistrationController.php` | POST `/api/register` with validation + entity creation |\n| `Infrastructure/Repository/DoctrineUserRepository.php` | Doctrine implementation of `UserRepository` |\n| `Infrastructure/Security/JWTSubscriber.php` | Adds roles to JWT payload on creation |\n\n**Verdict: User is the most complete bounded context. It establishes the pattern to follow.**\n\n#### 2c. `src/Shared/`\n\n| Directory | State |\n|-----------|-------|\n| `Domain/Entity/` | **EMPTY** — directory exists, no files |\n\n#### 2d. `src/Admin/`\n\n| Directory | State |\n|-----------|-------|\n| `Application/` | **EMPTY** |\n| `Domain/Entity/` | **EMPTY** — directory exists, no files |\n| `Infrastructure/` | **EMPTY** |\n\n#### 2e. `src/Controller/` (global controllers)\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `HealthController.php` | `GET /health` — returns `{\"status\":\"ok\"}` |\n\n#### 2f. Other `src/` files\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `Kernel.php` | Standard Symfony `MicroKernelTrait` kernel |\n| `Schedule.php` | Scheduler provider (empty, no tasks registered yet) |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Configuration Directory (`config/`)\n\n#### 3a. `config/packages/`\n\n| File | Key Content |\n|------|------------|\n| **`ai.yaml`** | **CRITICAL for Issue #3**. OpenRouter AI config: `base_url`, API key, `default_model: google/gemma-4-31b-it:free`, `fallback_model: meta-llama/llama-2-13b-chat:free`, `timeout: 60`, `max_tokens: 1000`, `temperature: 0.7`. ADR note: uses `symfony/http-client` directly, NOT `symfony/ai-bundle` (which doesn't exist on Packagist). |\n| **`messenger.yaml`** | 3 transports: `async` (env DSN, retry: 3 attempts, 2s delay, x2 multiplier), `failed` (Doctrine queue), `sync`. **No message routing configured yet.** |\n| **`security.yaml`** | Providers: `App\\User\\Domain\\Entity\\User`. Firewalls: `login` (JSON login on `/api/login`), `api` (JWT stateless). Access control: `/api/register` = PUBLIC, `/api/admin` = ROLE_ADMIN, `/api/triage` = ROLE_USER, `/api/*` = IS_AUTHENTICATED_FULLY. |\n| **`doctrine.yaml`** | Explicit entity mappings for all 4 contexts: Triage, User, Admin, Shared. `auto_mapping: false` — each entity dir must be registered manually. |\n| `lexik_jwt_authentication.yaml` | JWT keys from env vars |\n| `framework.yaml` | Session enabled, test config |\n| `nelmio_cors.yaml` | CORS from env |\n| `validator.yaml` | Basic validation config |\n\n#### 3b. `config/routes/`\n\n| File | Content |\n|------|---------|\n| `user.yaml` | Loads `#[Route]` attributes from `src/User/Infrastructure/Controller/` |\n| `framework.yaml` | Error pages in dev |\n| `security.yaml` | Logout route |\n| `routes.yaml` | Root — references `routing.controllers` |\n\n**Key observation: No `triage.yaml` or `admin.yaml` route file exists yet.** The User module has its own route file as a pattern to follow.\n\n#### 3c. `config/services.yaml`\n\n```yaml\nApp\\:\n    resource: '../src/'\n\nApp\\User\\Domain\\Repository\\UserRepository:\n    alias: App\\User\\Infrastructure\\Repository\\DoctrineUserRepository\n```\n\nFull autowiring + autoconfigure for `src/`. Explicit interface-to-implementation binding for `UserRepository`. **No Triage or Admin aliases defined yet.**\n\n---\n\n### 4. Migrations (`migrations/`)\n\nOnly one migration exists: **`Version20260529125614.php`** — creates the `users` table (id UUID, email unique, roles JSON, password, created_at). **No Triage table migration exists.**\n\n---\n\n### 5. Tests (`tests/`)\n\n| Path | Type | What it tests |\n|------|------|---------------|\n| `SmokeTest.php` | Unit | `assertTrue(true)` — bare minimum |\n| `User/Domain/Entity/UserTest.php` | Unit | Constructor, roles, promoteToAdmin idempotency, getUserIdentifier |\n| `User/Infrastructure/Controller/AuthControllerTest.php` | Functional (WebTestCase) | Login success, bad credentials, method check |\n| `User/Infrastructure/Controller/RegistrationControllerTest.php` | Functional | Success (201), duplicate email (422), invalid email (422), weak password (422) |\n| `User/Infrastructure/Repository/DoctrineUserRepositoryTest.php` | Integration (KernelTestCase) | Save+findById, findByEmail, null returns |\n| `User/Infrastructure/Security/JWTSubscriberTest.php` | Unit | Payload enrichment for user + admin roles |\n\n**No Triage tests exist.**\n\n---\n\n### 6. Established Patterns (from User module)\n\n1. **Entity Pattern:**\n   - `final class` with `#[ORM\\Entity]` and `#[ORM\\Table]`\n   - UUID v4 primary key via `Symfony\\Component\\Uid\\Uuid`\n   - `readonly` properties where possible (email, createdAt)\n   - Mutable properties only when needed (roles, password)\n   - Named constructor: `User::register()` static factory method\n   - Immutable: constructor sets id via `Uuid::v4()`, sets `createdAt` via `new \\DateTimeImmutable()`\n   - Timestamps: no auto-generated `#[ORM\\Column]` lifecycle callbacks; manual in constructor\n\n2. **Repository Pattern:**\n   - Interface in `Domain/Repository/` (e.g., `UserRepository`)\n   - Methods: `save()`, `findById()`, `findByEmail()`\n   - Doctrine implementation in `Infrastructure/Repository/Doctrine*Repository`\n   - Extends `ServiceEntityRepository`, implements domain interface\n   - Explicit alias binding in `services.yaml`\n\n3. **Controller Pattern:**\n   - `final class` extending `AbstractController` (when needing `$this->json()`) or standalone (HealthController)\n   - `#[Route]` attribute on each method\n   - `__invoke()` single-action controller style (RegistrationController)\n   - Route file per module in `config/routes/` (e.g., `user.yaml`)\n   - Validates input manually with `ValidatorInterface` + `Assert\\Collection`\n   - Returns JSON:API-ish format: `{\"data\": {\"id\": ..., \"type\": \"...\", \"attributes\": {...}}}`\n   - Error format: `{\"errors\": [{\"status\": \"422\", \"code\": \"...\", \"title\": \"...\", \"detail\": \"...\"}]}`\n\n4. **Security / Auth Pattern:**\n   - JWT via Lexik bundle\n   - Login firewall intercepts at `/api/login` (AuthController just exists for route reference)\n   - `JWTSubscriber` enriches payload with roles\n\n5. **Testing Pattern:**\n   - Unit tests extend `TestCase`, integration tests extend `KernelTestCase`, functional tests extend `WebTestCase`\n   - `uniqueEmail()` helper returns `'prefix-' . uniqid() . '@example.com'`\n   - API tests use `$client->jsonRequest()`\n\n---\n\n### 7. What is Missing for Issue #3 (Triage Interview)\n\nBased on `CONTEXT.md` (project glossary) and `agents.md` (architecture spec):\n\n| What needs building | Status |\n|---------------------|--------|\n| `TriageSubmission` entity (Domain/Entity/) | **Not started** — directory exists, no files |\n| `TriageSubmissionRepository` interface | **Not started** |\n| `DoctrineTriageSubmissionRepository` | **Not started** |\n| Conversation history storage (turns) | **Not started** — needs entity or embeddable |\n| Triage interview endpoint(s) | **Not started** — no controllers |\n| AI analyzer service | **Not started** — but `ai.yaml` config exists |\n| Messenger message for async AI calls | **Not started** — `messenger.yaml` routing is empty |\n| Route file (`config/routes/triage.yaml`) | **Not started** |\n| Service alias binding | **Not started** |\n| Migration for triage table(s) | **Not started** |\n| Tests for Triage | **Not started** |\n\n---\n\n### 8. Key Constraints from CONTEXT.md\n\n- **Single entity**: `TriageSubmission` contains everything — conversation history + final AI result (no separate `TriageResult`)\n- **No separate entity for \"turns\"** — conversation history is stored inline within the submission entity\n- **Character limits**: Initial Symptom Description = 500 chars, User answers = 300 chars, AI responses = 1000 chars\n- **Interview flow**: Submitter → Initial Symptom Description → up to 3 turns (AI question → user answer → AI response) → final result forced at turn 3 if needed\n- **`isSynthetic` flag** on submissions\n- **Naming**: Use \"Triage Submission\", \"Turn\", \"Conversation History\", \"Initial Symptom Description\" — NOT \"intake\", \"case\", \"chief complaint\"\n\n---\n\n### 9. Key Dependency Versions\n\nFrom `composer.json`: PHP >=8.2, Symfony 7.4.\\*, Doctrine ORM 3.6, `symfony/http-client` 7.4.\\* (for AI calls), `symfony/messenger` 7.4.\\*, `symfony/scheduler` 7.4.\\*, `lexik/jwt-authentication-bundle`, `nelmio/cors-bundle`. PHPUnit 11.5.55. PostgreSQL 16.\n</task_result>\n</task>",
