            "output": "<task id=\"ses_18b127ae9ffej7iK90eqA6d2GX\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI now have a complete picture of the entire frontend codebase. Here is my comprehensive summary:\n\n---\n\n## Comprehensive Frontend Codebase Summary\n\n### 1. Directory Structure\n\n```\nfrontend/src/\n├── api/\n│   ├── client.ts          # Axios instance with JWT interceptors\n│   ├── endpoints.ts       # All API endpoint paths as constants\n│   └── types.ts           # All TypeScript interfaces for API payloads\n├── components/\n│   ├── layout/\n│   │   ├── AdminRoute.tsx       # Route guard (checks isAdmin)\n│   │   ├── AppLayout.tsx        # Shell: Header + <Outlet/>\n│   │   ├── Header.tsx           # Nav: TriageFlow logo, nav links, login/logout\n│   │   └── ProtectedRoute.tsx   # Route guard (checks JWT in localStorage)\n│   ├── shared/\n│   │   ├── EmptyState.tsx       # Icon + title + description + optional action slot\n│   │   ├── ErrorBoundary.tsx    # Class-based error boundary with \"Try again\" button\n│   │   └── Loader.tsx           # Spinner + message centered\n│   └── ui/\n│       ├── Badge.tsx            # Status/urgency pill (pending, processing, completed, failed, low, medium, high, emergency)\n│       ├── Button.tsx           # Three variants (primary/secondary/danger), three sizes, loading state\n│       ├── Card.tsx             # Rounded bordered container with shadow\n│       ├── Input.tsx            # forwardRef input with label and error message\n│       └── Spinner.tsx          # SVG spinner, three sizes\n├── features/\n│   ├── admin/pages/\n│   │   ├── DashboardPage.tsx        # STUB: \"Admin Dashboard\" heading only\n│   │   ├── SubmissionDetailPage.tsx # STUB: \"Submission Detail\" heading only\n│   │   └── UsersPage.tsx            # STUB: \"Users\" heading only\n│   ├── auth/pages/\n│   │   ├── LoginPage.tsx       # FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n│   │   └── RegisterPage.tsx    # FULLY IMPLEMENTED\n│   ├── submissions/pages/\n│   │   └── MySubmissionsPage.tsx    # STUB: \"My Submissions\" heading only\n│   └── triage/\n│       ├── components/         # EMPTY — ready for Issue #3\n│       ├── hooks/              # EMPTY — ready for Issue #3\n│       └── pages/\n│           ├── TriagePage.tsx       # STUB: \"Triage\" heading only\n│           └── TriageResultPage.tsx # STUB: \"Triage Result\" heading only\n├── hooks/\n│   └── useAuth.ts             # Auth state + login/logout actions, JWT role detection\n├── lib/                       # EMPTY\n├── styles/\n│   └── index.css              # Tailwind v4 import + custom theme colors + dark mode variant\n├── test/\n│   └── setup.ts               # jest-dom matchers for vitest\n├── App.tsx                    # Thin wrapper: <RouterProvider router={router} />\n├── main.tsx                   # Entry: React.StrictMode + QueryClientProvider + App\n├── routes.tsx                 # All route definitions (createBrowserRouter)\n└── vite-env.d.ts              # Vite client type reference\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Routes (`src/routes.tsx`)\n\nAll routes live under `<AppLayout />`:\n\n| Path | Component | Guard | Load Strategy |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `/` | Redirect → `/triage` | None | - |\n| `/login` | LoginPage | None | Lazy (code-split) |\n| `/register` | RegisterPage | None | Lazy (code-split) |\n| `/triage` | TriagePage | ProtectedRoute (JWT check) | Direct import |\n| `/triage/:id/result` | TriageResultPage | ProtectedRoute | Direct import |\n| `/submissions` | MySubmissionsPage | ProtectedRoute | Direct import |\n| `/admin` | DashboardPage | AdminRoute (isAdmin check) | Lazy |\n| `/admin/submissions/:id` | SubmissionDetailPage | AdminRoute | Lazy |\n| `/admin/users` | UsersPage | AdminRoute | Lazy |\n\n**Key observation**: The three pages for Issue #3 (TriagePage, TriageResultPage, MySubmissionsPage) are **directly imported** (not lazy-loaded), unlike auth and admin pages.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Stubs to Replace (Issue #3 Targets)\n\nAll three stubs are **identical one-liners**:\n\n**TriagePage** (`/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/src/features/triage/pages/TriagePage.tsx`):\n```tsx\nexport function TriagePage() {\n  return <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100\">Triage</h1>;\n}\n```\n\n**TriageResultPage** (`/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/src/features/triage/pages/TriageResultPage.tsx`):\n```tsx\nexport function TriageResultPage() {\n  return <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100\">Triage Result</h1>;\n}\n```\n\n**MySubmissionsPage** (`/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/src/features/submissions/pages/MySubmissionsPage.tsx`):\n```tsx\nexport function MySubmissionsPage() {\n  return <h1 className=\"text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100\">My Submissions</h1>;\n}\n```\n\nEmpty directories exist waiting for new files:\n- `/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/src/features/triage/components/` (empty)\n- `/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/src/features/triage/hooks/` (empty)\n\n---\n\n### 4. API Client Setup\n\n**Axios instance** (`src/api/client.ts`):\n- Base URL from `VITE_API_URL` env var (defaults to `http://localhost:8000`)\n- Request interceptor: attaches `Bearer <token>` from `localStorage('jwt_token')`\n- Response interceptor: on 401, clears token and redirects to `/login` (unless already there)\n\n**Endpoints** (`src/api/endpoints.ts`):\n```ts\nTRIAGE: {\n  SUBMIT: '/api/triage/submit',\n  STATUS: (id: string) => `/api/triage/status/${id}`,\n  ANSWER: (id: string) => `/api/triage/${id}/answer`,\n  RESULT: (id: string) => `/api/triage/result/${id}`,\n  MY_SUBMISSIONS: '/api/triage/submissions',\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. TypeScript Types (`src/api/types.ts`)\n\nAll types are `readonly` (immutable pattern). Key ones relevant to Issue #3:\n\n```ts\n// The conversation message in the interview transcript\nConversationMessage {\n  role: 'user' | 'assistant';\n  content: string;\n  type: 'initial_description' | 'follow_up' | 'answer' | 'result';\n  timestamp: string;\n}\n\n// The full triage submission entity\nTriageSubmissionResource {\n  id: string;\n  type: 'triage_submission';\n  attributes: {\n    status: 'pending' | 'processing' | 'completed' | 'failed';\n    isSynthetic: boolean;\n    specialist: string | null;\n    urgency: 'EMERGENCY' | 'HIGH' | 'MEDIUM' | 'LOW' | null;\n    justification: string | null;\n    conversationHistory: readonly ConversationMessage[];\n    processingDuration: number | null;\n    submittedAt: string;\n    processedAt: string | null;\n  };\n}\n\n// Polling status (lightweight)\nTriageStatusResource {\n  id: string;\n  type: 'triage_submission';\n  attributes: {\n    status: 'pending' | 'processing' | 'completed' | 'failed';\n    currentTurn: number;\n    lastAssistantMessage: string | null;\n  };\n}\n\n// Request/response shapes\nSubmitTriageRequest { initialDescription: string }\nSubmitTriageResponse { data: { id, type, attributes: { status, submittedAt } } }\nTriageAnswerRequest { content: string }\nTriageAnswerResponse { data: { id, type, attributes: { status } } }\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. `useAuth` Hook\n\nLocated at `/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/src/hooks/useAuth.ts`:\n- Reads JWT from `localStorage('jwt_token')` on init\n- Decodes JWT payload to determine `isAdmin` (checks for `ROLE_ADMIN` in `roles`)\n- Returns `{ isAuthenticated, isAdmin, token, login(token), logout() }`\n- `login` stores token + updates state; `logout` removes token + resets state\n- **Used in**: AppLayout (passes to Header), AdminRoute, LoginPage\n\n---\n\n### 7. Dependencies (`package.json`)\n\n**Runtime**:\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| react + react-dom | ^19.2.6 | UI library |\n| react-router-dom | ^7.16.0 | Client-side routing |\n| @tanstack/react-query | ^5.100.14 | Server state / data fetching |\n| axios | ^1.16.1 | HTTP client |\n| clsx | ^2.1.1 | Conditional className builder |\n\n**Dev**:\n- TypeScript ~6.0.2 (strict mode, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `verbatimModuleSyntax`, `erasableSyntaxOnly`)\n- Vite ^8.0.12 + @vitejs/plugin-react\n- Tailwind CSS ^4.3.0 (via @tailwindcss/vite plugin)\n- Vitest ^4.1.7 + @testing-library/react + jsdom\n- ESLint ^10.3.0 with react-hooks and react-refresh plugins\n\n---\n\n### 8. Patterns Used\n\n**Data fetching pattern** (from LoginPage/RegisterPage):\n- `useMutation` from `@tanstack/react-query`\n- `mutationFn` calls `apiClient.post<T>(endpoint, payload).then(r => r.data)`\n- `onSuccess` / `onError` callbacks handle navigation and error state\n- Local `useState` for form fields, `useNavigate` for redirect\n\n**Component patterns**:\n- All components are **named function exports** (no default exports)\n- Props interfaces are `readonly` and defined inline above the component\n- `clsx` is used for conditional class composition\n- Tailwind utility classes, with `dark:` prefix for dark mode\n- Size variants use object maps or ternary expressions\n- `forwardRef` used for form inputs (Input.tsx)\n\n**Styling**:\n- Tailwind v4 with `@import \"tailwindcss\"` and `@variant dark`\n- Custom CSS theme variables for primary and urgency colors\n- Dark mode via `dark:` utility classes throughout\n\n**Route guards**:\n- `ProtectedRoute`: reads `localStorage` directly (not useAuth hook), redirects to `/login`\n- `AdminRoute`: uses `useAuth().isAdmin`, redirects to `/`\n- Both render `<Outlet />` when authorized\n\n**Routing**:\n- Flat route tree nested under AppLayout\n- Mix of direct imports (triage pages) and lazy `import()` (auth, admin pages)\n- Index route redirects `/` → `/triage`\n\n**TypeScript**:\n- Strict mode with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` and `verbatimModuleSyntax`\n- All interfaces use `readonly` properties\n- No `enum` — string literal unions used instead\n\n---\n\n### 9. What Exists vs. What Needs Building for Issue #3\n\n**Already exists and ready to use:**\n- Full API client with JWT auth and all triage endpoint definitions\n- Complete TypeScript types for all triage-related request/response shapes\n- UI component library (Button, Card, Badge, Input, Spinner)\n- Shared components (Loader, EmptyState, ErrorBoundary)\n- Route definitions already wired up (TriagePage, TriageResultPage, MySubmissionsPage)\n- Empty `features/triage/components/` and `features/triage/hooks/` directories\n\n**Needs to be built for Issue #3:**\n1. **TriagePage** — The interview flow: initial symptom input → conversation display → answer input → polling for AI response\n2. **TriageResultPage** — Displays the completed triage result: urgency badge, specialist recommendation, justification, full conversation history\n3. **MySubmissionsPage** — Lists all user's submissions with status badges, links to results\n4. **Custom hooks** (in `features/triage/hooks/`) — e.g., `useTriageInterview`, `useTriagePolling`, `useSubmissions`\n5. **Triage components** (in `features/triage/components/`) — e.g., `ConversationThread`, `MessageBubble`, `InitialSymptomForm`, `AnswerInput`, `UrgencyIndicator`, `SubmissionCard`\n</task_result>\n</task>",
