gents.md shows `$symptoms` as an array, separate `$urgency`, `$specialist` etc.\n   - CONTEXT.md says conversation history is stored in the entity — but as what? JSON column? Array of objects?\n   - Frontend types define `ConversationMessage` with `role`, `content`, `type`, `timestamp`\n   - The handoff says \"conversationHistory (json)\"\n\n5. **Endpoints**: The handoff lists 5 endpoints. But some of these:\n   - `POST /api/triage/submit` — submit initial symptom\n   - `POST /api/triage/{id}/answer` — answer AI follow-up\n   - `GET /api/triage/status/{id}` — poll for status\n   - `GET /api/triage/result/{id}` — get final result\n   - `GET /api/triage/submissions` — list user's submissions\n   \n   The question is: are these synchronous or async? The handoff says \"dispatches async Message\". But the conversation flow seems interactive — user submits, AI responds, user answers, AI asks follow-up... If it's truly async (Messenger), the user experience might suffer because there's a polling loop between each turn.\n\n6. **Entity status enum**: `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed`. But with a multi-turn conversation, what does \"processing\" mean? Is it processing between turns? Or only for the initial submission?\n\n7. **Turn counting**: The CONTEXT.md says \"up to 3 Turns\". How is this tracked? In the entity? In a separate field?\n\n8. **The Turn mechanism**: The AI can produce a final result in any Turn (1, 2, or 3) or be forced at Turn 3. This means the AI response could be EITHER a follow-up question OR a final triage result. How do we differentiate between \"here's another question\" vs \"here's the final result\"?\n\n9. **Synthetic Cases**: Not part of Issue #3, but the entity needs the `isSynthetic` flag from day 1.\n\nLet me now start the grilling session with the most critical question first — the entity model vs. the conversation flow.\n\nActually, wait — the grill-with-docs skill says to ask questions ONE AT A TIME, waiting for feedback. Let me s