        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "From a senior perspective: **yes, the single-entity approach is the correct pattern** — but not because it's simpler. It's correct because the domain model demands it.\n\nHere's the reasoning:\n\n---\n\n### The Triage Result is a Value, not an Entity\n\nIn DDD terms, an **entity** has:\n- Its own identity (UUID/ID)\n- An independent lifecycle (created, modified, deleted separately)\n- Independent queries (you'd fetch TriageResults without TriageSubmissions)\n\nA Triage Result has **none of these**. It has no meaningful identity apart from the submission. You'd never query \"all triage results\" without their submissions. You'd never delete or modify a result independently. It's born when the submission is processed and dies when the submission dies.\n\nThat makes it a **value object** within the TriageSubmission aggregate — not a separate entity.\n\n---\n\n### Three patterns, ranked:\n\n| Pattern | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| **Separate `TriageResult` entity** with FK to `TriageSubmission` | **Wrong.** Creates entity with no independent identity. Over-normalization for a 1:1 relationship that's always read together. |\n| **Loose nullable fields** (`$specialist`, `$urgency`, `$justification`) directly on `TriageSubmission` | **Acceptable but weak.** Scatters a cohesive concept. No enforcement that all three are either present or absent together. |\n| **Doctrine Embeddable** `TriageOutcome` with those three fields, nullable on the parent | **Best.** Maintains the domain concept that the outcome is a cohesive unit. Type-safe — you either have a complete `TriageOutcome` or `null`. Maps to the same table, no join. |\n\n---\n\n### My recommendation:\n\nSingle entity — `TriageSubmission` — with:\n- `$conversationHistory`: JSON column (bounded to ~5KB by character limits, perfectly fine)\n- `$outcome`: **nullable Embeddable** (`TriageOutcome`) containing `specialist`, `urgency`, `justification`\n\nThis is the pattern the frontend types already encode. The `backend/agents.md` spec showing a separate `TriageResult.php` file is out-of-date and should be corrected.\n\nAgree? If so, next question: the Turn/async flow design.",
