        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Good. Let me correct `backend/agents.md` when we do the implementation. Next question:\n\n---\n\n**Question 2: Async (Messenger + Polling) vs Synchronous — the Turn Flow**\n\nThe handoff doc and its dependency graph call for Messenger-based async processing (`ProcessTriageMessage` dispatched on every AI call, frontend polls `GET /api/triage/status/{id}`). This gives us a flow like:\n\n```\nUser submits → pending → [Messenger] → processing → awaiting_answer\nUser answers → [Messenger] → processing → awaiting_answer (or → completed)\n```\n\nThe frontend types already encode this: `TriageStatusResource` returns `status`, `currentTurn`, `lastAssistantMessage` — clearly built for polling.\n\nThe alternative is synchronous HTTP calls to OpenRouter per turn (block the PHP request for 2-4 seconds, return the result directly).\n\n**Trade-offs:**\n\n| | Async (Messenger) | Sync (HTTP block) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **UX** | Spinner/polling between turns | Simpler: user waits, sees response |\n| **Resilience** | Retry on failure, dead letter queue | No retry unless frontend retries |\n| **Architecture** | Proper separation, scales to synthetic cases | Single-threaded, blocks worker |\n| **Demo feel** | Feels more \"enterprise\" | Feels more \"app-like\" |\n| **Complexity** | More moving parts (consumer, polling, state machine) | Simpler: request → response |\n| **Alignment** | Matches existing frontend types + handoff plan | Would need frontend redesign |\n\n**My recommendation**: Stick with async + Messenger. The frontend types and API surface are already designed for it. For a portfolio demo, the \"your case is being analyzed\" spinner between turns actually reinforces the medical-analysis narrative. And it's the same architecture synthetic cases will use in Issue #6.\n\nDo you agree with the async approach? If so, next question: the status state machine — specifically, what happens between turns.\n\n",
