        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Good. Let me capture the decisions so far mentally: single entity with `TriageOutcome` embeddable, async Messenger, 5-state machine (`pending → processing → awaiting_answer → processing → ... → completed`).\n\n---\n\n**Question 4: AI Response Discrimination — Question vs Final Result**\n\nThe AI produces one of two things on each turn:\n1. **A follow-up question** — e.g., \"How long have you had these headaches? Are they worse in the morning?\"\n2. **A final triage result** — specialist, urgency, justification\n\nThe backend needs to know which one it received. Two approaches:\n\n| Approach | How it works | Risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **A. JSON discrimination** | System prompt instructs AI to always output JSON: `{\"type\":\"question\",\"content\":\"...\"}` or `{\"type\":\"result\",\"specialist\":\"...\",\"urgency\":\"...\",\"justification\":\"...\"}`. Backend parses `type` field. | Free models (Gemma, Llama-2) may sometimes forget the JSON format. Need validation fallback. |\n| **B. Separate system prompts** | Two AI calls: first with \"ask a follow-up question\" prompt, then decide based on turn count whether to also call with \"give me a result\" prompt. or distinguish by `currentTurn >= 3` → force result. | Double the API calls, doubles cost and latency. |\n\n**My recommendation**: **Approach A** — JSON discrimination in a single call. The system prompt explicitly constrains output format. On malformed JSON (no `type` field, unparseable), treat as `type: \"question\"` with the raw text as content (don't lose data). At `currentTurn >= 3`, instruct the prompt to ONLY return `{\"type\":\"result\",...}` — the force logic lives in the prompt, not in backend branching.\n\nBackend flow per turn:\n```\nAI response → json_decode → \n  type=question  → append to conversation, set status=awaiting_answer, increment turn\n  type=result    → extract outcome, persist to embeddable, set status=completed\n  malformed JSON → treat as question with rawText\n```\n\n