        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Noted — we'll check OpenRouter's structured output / JSON mode support during implementation. On to the next branch:\n\n---\n\n**Question 5: Conversation History — JSON Column Shape**\n\nThe frontend `ConversationMessage` type defines:\n\n```ts\n{ role: 'user' | 'assistant'; content: string; type: 'initial_description' | 'follow_up' | 'answer' | 'result'; timestamp: string }\n```\n\nThat's 4 fields per message × ~10 messages (initial + up to 3 turns × 3 messages per turn: question, answer, question/result) ≈ ~10 rows. Well within JSON column sanity.\n\nBut I see redundancy: `role` (`user`/`assistant`) and `type` overlap. An `initial_description` is always `user`. A `follow_up` is always `assistant`. An `answer` is always `user`. A `result` is always `assistant`.\n\n**My recommendation**: Drop `role` from the persisted shape. `type` already encodes who said it. Cleaner:\n\n```php\n// Each entry in the JSON column\n[\n    'type'      => 'initial_description' | 'follow_up' | 'answer' | 'result',\n    'content'   => string,\n    'timestamp' => ISO 8601 string,\n]\n```\n\nFour `type` values map cleanly to the state machine:\n- `initial_description` → submitted by user, starts the pipeline\n- `follow_up` → AI question, causes `status = awaiting_answer`\n- `answer` → user response, triggers next Messenger dispatch\n- `result` → final AI output, causes `status = completed` + sets `TriageOutcome`\n\nThe frontend can still map `type` to visual role at display time — user-bubble for `initial_description`/`answer`, assistant-bubble for `follow_up`/`result`.\n\nAgree to drop `role` from the persisted shape?\n\n\n\n",
