          "text": "Let me now continue with the next question. We've covered:\n1. Single entity with TriageOutcome embeddable\n2. Async + Messenger\n3. 5-state machine: pending, processing, awaiting_answer, completed, failed\n4. JSON discrimination for AI responses\n5. Drop `role` from conversation, keep `type`\n6. Explicit `currentTurn` field\n7. Keep 5 endpoints, separate status vs result\n8. Wrapped OpenRouterClient abstraction\n9. Single page interview flow\n\nWhat's left to grill? Let me think about what the handoff lists and what tensions remain:\n\n- The system prompt design (specialists list, urgency levels)\n- Character limits enforcement (where? frontend? backend? both?)\n- Error handling patterns (AI timeout, malformed JSON, 3-turn force fallback)\n- The Messenger message + handler structure\n- How to test without calling real AI (mocking strategy)\n- The conversation history truncation for system prompt (how much context does the AI get?)\n- The `lastAssistantMessage` field on the status response - how to derive it\n\nLet me ask about the system prompt next, then Messenger structure, then error handling.",
