        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\n**Question 10: System Prompt — Where and How?**\n\nThe AI needs a system prompt instructing it to act as a medical triage assistant. `backend/agents.md` has a template (lines 192-202) that defines 8 specialists, 4 urgency levels, JSON output format, and the demo disclaimer. But with our modified strategy (JSON discrimination: `type: question` vs `type: result`), this prompt needs updating.\n\nTwo questions in one:\n\n**A. Where does the prompt live?** Options:\n- Hardcoded in `TriageAnalyzer` (simple, 1 class)\n- Separate `TriageSystemPrompt` service/class (testable, swappable for synthetic vs real)\n- Config parameter in `ai.yaml` (editable without code change)\n\n**B. What should it say?** The existing template doesn't handle multi-turn conversation. The prompt needs to understand:\n- Turn number: \"You are on turn X of 3\"\n- Discriminated output: `type: question` vs `type: result`\n- Force result at turn 3: \"This is your final turn — you MUST return a result\"\n- Conversation history: the full transcript so far\n\n**My recommendation:**\n- **Location**: `TriageSystemPrompt` service class in `App\\Triage\\Application\\Service\\`. Not a config parameter — the prompt is logic, not configuration. Inject via DI so it can be tested and swapped.\n- **Content**: Template with placeholders for `{currentTurn}`, `{maxTurns}`, `{forceResult}`, `{conversationHistory}`. The `TriageAnalyzer` populates these and sends to `OpenRouterClient`.\n\nRevised output format in the prompt:\n```json\n{\"type\": \"question\", \"content\": \"How long have you had these symptoms?\"}\n// OR\n{\"type\": \"result\", \"specialist\": \"NEUROLOGIST\", \"urgency\": \"HIGH\", \"justification\": \"Patient reports severe recurring headaches with...\"}\n```\n\nIf `currentTurn >= maxTurns`, the prompt variant says: \"You've asked enough questions. You MUST return a result now.\"\n\nAgree on `TriageSystemPrompt` as a separate service?\n\n\n\n",
