        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Good. Now let me cover the remaining design branches:\n\n---\n\n**Question 12: Character Limits — Where to Enforce?**\n\nCONTEXT.md defines: Initial Symptom Description ≤ 500, User answers ≤ 300, AI responses ≤ 1000 chars.\n\nThree enforcement points:\n\n| Point | What |\n|---|---|\n| **Frontend** | `maxLength` on textarea, character counter. Soft UX guard. |\n| **Backend controller** | Symfony Validator constraint on submit/answer DTOs. Hard guard — 422 if exceeded. |\n| **System prompt** | Instruct AI: \"Keep responses under 1000 characters.\" No enforcement, but best-effort guidance. |\n\n**My recommendation**: Enforce at all three. Frontend for UX (show counter \"287/300\"), backend for integrity (never trust the client), and prompt for AI conciseness (prevent token bloat). The backend is the authoritative gate — if somehow a message exceeds the limit, return 422 with a clear error. The AI's response length can't be enforced server-side (we can truncate, but that's worse), so the prompt instruction is our best tool.\n\nAgree?\n\n\n\n",
