          "text": "Let me continue with the remaining questions. We've covered a lot of ground. Let me think about what design branches remain:\n\n1. ✅ Single entity (TriageSubmission with TriageOutcome embeddable)\n2. ✅ Async + Messenger\n3. ✅ 5-state status machine\n4. ✅ JSON discrimination (type: question vs result)\n5. ✅ Dropped `role` from conversation history\n6. ✅ Explicit `currentTurn` field\n7. ✅ Separate status and result endpoints\n8. ✅ Single page interview flow\n9. ✅ TriageSystemPrompt as separate service\n10. ✅ OpenRouterClient wrapper\n11. ✅ Revised implementation order\n12. ✅ Character limits enforced at 3 points\n\nRemaining branches:\n- Error handling: What happens when OpenRouter is down, returns garbage, times out?\n- The ProcessTriageMessage shape: what data does it carry?\n- The SubmitTriageCommand shape: what data?\n- Testing strategy: how to mock OpenRouter in tests?\n- The `lastAssistantMessage` in status response: what exactly does it return?\n- The MySubmissionsPage endpoint: authenticated filter + pagination?\n- Frontend types: need to update the ConversationMessage to drop `role`\n- The exact specialist list\n\nLet me continue with the next critical question.",
