        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\n**Question 13: Error Resilience — What Happens When AI Fails?**\n\nOpenRouter can fail in several ways: network timeout, 429 rate limit, malformed JSON response, empty response. The Messenger setup has 3 retries with exponential backoff — but what happens after 3 failures?\n\nThree failure scenarios and options:\n\n| Failure | Option A (Fail Submission) | Option B (Graceful Degrade) |\n|---|---|---|\n| All 3 retries exhausted | `status = failed`, store error message. User sees \"Analysis failed, please try again.\" | N/A — can't recover |\n| Malformed JSON (no `type` field) | `status = failed`, log raw response for debugging | Treat as `type: question` with raw text as content. User still sees something. |\n| Turn-3 force result but AI returns `type: question` | `status = failed` — violated instruction | Parse anyway: if JSON has `specialist`/`urgency`/`justification`, treat it as a result. Otherwise fail. |\n\n**My recommendation**: \n- **3 retries exhausted** → `status = failed`, store error message, user sees failure UI with \"Try again\" button. This is Option A (only option).\n- **Malformed JSON on turns 1-2** → Option B: treat as question with raw text. Better to show the user *something* conversational than a hard failure. The raw text is still medically themed even if unparseable.\n- **Turn-3 force but AI still returns question** → Option A: `status = failed`. The system gave a firm instruction and the model didn't comply. Better to fail explicitly than silently accept a non-result as final.\n\nThe `ProcessTriageMessage` handler needs to catch `Throwable` from the AI call and decide: increment retry count and re-throw (Messenger handles retry), or set `status = failed` and move to failed queue.\n\nAgree with this error strategy?\n\n\n\n",
