        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\n**Question 14: Frontend Hooks — What Custom Hooks Do We Need?**\n\nThe interview state machine on `/triage` needs to manage: form submission, polling, answer submission, navigation to result. Raw `useMutation` + `useQuery` can handle this, but wrapping in custom hooks keeps the page component clean.\n\n**My recommendation** — two hooks:\n\n```ts\n// features/triage/hooks/useTriageInterview.ts\n// Manages the full interview lifecycle\n// Returns: { state, submitSymptom, submitAnswer, conversation, currentTurn }\n// state: 'idle' | 'submitting' | 'polling' | 'awaiting_answer' | 'submitting_answer' | 'redirecting'\n\n// features/triage/hooks/useTriagePolling.ts\n// Polls GET /api/triage/status/{id} with refetchInterval\n// Returns: { status, currentTurn, lastAssistantMessage }\n// Used inside useTriageInterview\n```\n\n`useTriageInterview` is the primary hook. It composes `useTriagePolling` internally. The page component just calls `useTriageInterview()` and renders based on `state`.\n\nFor `MySubmissionsPage`, a simpler `useQuery` directly fetching `GET /api/triage/submissions` is sufficient — no custom hook needed unless we want pagination.\n\nFor `TriageResultPage`, `useQuery` fetching `GET /api/triage/result/{id}` — also simple enough to call directly.\n\nAgree on this hook structure?\n\n\n\n",
