          "type": "text",
          "text": "Almost done. A few more branches to cover:\n\n---\n\n**Question 15: Authorization — Can a Malicious User Answer Another User's Submission?**\n\n`POST /api/triage/{id}/answer` takes a submission ID from the URL. Without an ownership check, User A could answer User B's submission by guessing the UUID.\n\nSecurity is straightforward since UUIDs aren't guessable, but for a portfolio project that demonstrates competency, we should enforce ownership.\n\n**My recommendation**: In `TriageController::answer`, after loading the submission by ID, assert `$submission->getUser()->getId() === $this->getUser()->getId()` or return 403. Same for `GET /api/triage/status/{id}` and `GET /api/triage/result/{id}`. For `GET /api/triage/submissions`, query by the authenticated user's ID — the repository method takes a `Uuid $userId` parameter and scopes the query.\n\nThe `User` entity doesn't have a `getSubmissions()` collection — which is correct (no bidirectional traversal across bounded contexts in DDD light). The repository handles the scoping instead.\n\nAgree?\n\n\n\n",
