              "prompt": "Load context from .tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue3-triage/context.md\n\nRead the context file for full requirements, standards, constraints, and the 5-batch implementation order.\n\nBreak this feature into atomic JSON subtasks. Create .tmp/tasks/issue3-triage/task.json + subtask_NN.json files.\n\nCRITICAL DESIGN DECISIONS (from grill-with-docs session):\n- Single TriageSubmission entity with TriageOutcome Doctrine Embeddable (NOT separate entity)\n- 5-state status machine: pending → processing → awaiting_answer → processing → ... → completed (plus failed)\n- AI via OpenRouter HTTP client directly (no symfony/ai-bundle)\n- JSON discrimination: {\"type\":\"question\"} vs {\"type\":\"result\",\"specialist\":\"...\",\"urgency\":\"...\",\"justification\":\"...\"}\n- Conversation history: {type, content, timestamp} (no role field - type encodes it)\n- Explicit $currentTurn int field, force result at turn >= 3\n- 5 endpoints: POST submit, POST answer, GET status, GET result, GET submissions(all deferred but endpoint wired)\n- OpenRouterClient (Shared), TriageSystemPrompt (service), TriageAnalyzer (service)\n- Ownership check on all endpoints\n- ManyToOne to User entity\n- Frontend: single-page interview state machine, navigate to result on complete\n- Character limits: 500/300/1000 chars, enforced frontend + backend + prompt\n- MySubmissionsPage DEFERRED - not in Issue #3\n- TDD mandatory: write tests first, RED → GREEN → REFACTOR\n- Symfony 7.4, PHP 8.4, React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind v4\n\nIMPLEMENTATION ORDER (5 batches, batches 1-4 sequential, batch 5 parallel to 4):\n```\nBatch 1: Foundation\n  - TriageOutcome embeddable + TriageStatus enum\n  - TriageSubmission entity\n  - TriageSubmissionRepository interface + Doctrine impl\n  - Migration\n  - services.yaml binding\n\nBatch 2: AI Layer\n  - OpenRouterClient (in Shared\\Infrastructure\\Ai\\)\n  - TriageSystemPrompt service\n  - TriageAnalyzer service\n\nBatch 3: Pipeline\n  - SubmitTriageCommand + Handler\n  - ProcessTriageMessage (Messenger)\n  - Messenger routing config\n\nBatch 4: Controllers\n  - config/routes/triage.yaml\n  - TriageController (5 endpoints)\n\nBatch 5: Frontend (parallel, independent)\n  - Update types (new status, drop role)\n  - TriagePage (interview state machine)\n  - TriageResultPage\n```\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- context_files in each subtask = ONLY standards paths (from ## Context Files section)\n- reference_files in each subtask = ONLY source/project files (from ## Reference Files section)\n- Do NOT mix standards and source files in the same array.\n- Mark isolated tasks within the same batch as parallel: true (frontend and backend can be parallel)\n- Backend batches must be sequential (1→2→3→4), but batch 5 can run parallel to batch 4\n- Include TDD checkpoint steps (write test → RED → implement → GREEN → refactor) in each subtask\n- Each subtask should produce a small, testable, committable unit of work"
