                  "summary": "## Grill-with-Docs Session: Issue #3 Triage Interview\n\nUser invoked `/grill-with-docs` for the Triage Interview implementation. 18 questions resolved across the full design tree:\n\n### Key Decisions (all user-approved):\n1. **Entity model**: Single `TriageSubmission` with `TriageOutcome` Doctrine Embeddable (NOT separate entity). TriageOutcome is a value object — null only at parent entity level.\n2. **Async flow**: Messenger-based with 5-state machine: `pending → processing → awaiting_answer → ... → completed` (+ `failed`). Explicit `$currentTurn` int field.\n3. **AI response discrimination**: JSON with `{\"type\":\"question\"}` vs `{\"type\":\"result\",\"specialist\":\"...\",\"urgency\":\"...\",\"justification\":\"...\"}`. Approach A with structured output.\n4. **Conversation history**: JSON column, entries: `{type, content, timestamp}`. Dropped `role` — `type` encodes who said it (initial_description=user, question=assistant, answer=user, result=assistant).\n5. **AI layer**: `OpenRouterClient` (Shared\\Infrastructure\\Ai) wraps `symfony/http-client`. `TriageSystemPrompt` + `TriageAnalyzer` as separate services. ADR 0002 confirmed: no symfony/ai-bundle.\n6. **Frontend**: Single-page interview state machine on `/triage`, navigate to `/triage/:id/result` on complete. `useTriageInterview` hook composing `useTriagePolling`.\n7. **Character limits**: Frontend maxLength + backend Validator (hard gate) + system prompt (AI guidance). 500/300/1000 chars.\n8. **Error strategy**: 3 Messenger retries → failed. Malformed JSON on turns 1-2 → treat as question. Turn 3 force non-compliance → failed.\n9. **Authorization**: Ownership check on all endpoints (403 if user mismatch). ManyToOne to User.\n10. **MySubmissionsPage**: DEFERRED to later issue.\n11. **Turn counting**: `$currentTurn` starts at 0. Incremented on AI question. Force result at turn ≥ 3.\n12. **Specialists**: No enum exists in code yet — will use string-based with TriageSystemPrompt defining the list.\n\n### CONTEXT.md Updated\nAdded `TriageOutcome` term: \"The final AI analysis within a Triage Submission — not a separate entity. Contains specialist, urgency, and justification. Is null while the interview is in progress.\"\n\n### Implementation Order\n5 batches: Foundation (4 tasks) → AI Layer (3 tasks) → Pipeline (3 tasks) → Controllers (2 tasks) → Frontend (3 tasks). Batches 1-4 sequential backend. Batch 5 parallel to 4."
                },
                {
                  "startId": "m0045",
                  "endId": "m0051",
                  "summary": "## Session Initialization\n\nCreated `.tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue3-triage/context.md` with all decisions, context files, reference files, and 5-batch implementation plan. Loaded `code-quality.md` (mandatory).\n\nTaskManager created 15 subtasks in `.tmp/tasks/issue3-triage/`:\n- Batch 1 (tasks 01-04): Foundation — TriageStatus, TriageOutcome, TriageSubmission, repository, migration\n- Batch 2 (tasks 05-07): AI Layer — OpenRouterClient, TriageSystemPrompt, TriageAnalyzer\n- Batch 3 (tasks 08-10): Pipeline — SubmitTriageCommand/Handler, ProcessTriageMessage, Messenger routing\n- Batch 4 (tasks 11-12): Controllers — routes, TriageController endpoints\n- Batch 5 (tasks 13-15): Frontend — types update, TriagePage, TriageResultPage\n\nTask 01 + 13 can run in parallel (backend foundation + frontend types). Loaded tdd-workflow skill."
                },
                {
                  "startId": "m0052",
