            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/docs/adr/0002-custom-ai-no-bundle.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Custom AI integration — no symfony/ai-bundle\n2: \n3: The plan assumed `symfony/ai-bundle` would provide an `ai:` YAML config key with platform/agent autowiring. As of 2026-05, no such package exists on Packagist.\n4: \n5: AI calls are implemented via `symfony/http-client` directly, using a custom `config/packages/ai.yaml` for OpenRouter parameters (base URL, API key, default/fallback model, timeout, max_tokens, temperature). The config lives in `parameters.ai.openrouter.*` — not a bundle-owned config tree.\n6: \n7: If a stable `symfony/ai-bundle` ships later, the migration path is:\n8: \n9: 1. Replace `parameters:` block with `ai:` config tree\n10: 2. Swap manual HTTP Client calls for bundle-injected AI service\n11: 3. Remove custom service wiring\n12: \n13: Until then, the `ai.yaml` comment block documents this as a deliberate architectural deviation.\n\n(End of file - total 13 lines)\n</content>",
            "metadata": {
              "preview": "# Custom AI integration — no symfony/ai-bundle\n\nThe plan assumed `symfony/ai-bundle` would provide an `ai:` YAML config key with platform/agent autowiring. As of 2026-05, no such package exists on Packagist.\n\nAI calls are implemented via `symfony/http-client` directly, using a custom `config/packages/ai.yaml` for OpenRouter parameters (base URL, API key, default/fallback model, timeout, max_tokens, temperature). The config lives in `parameters.ai.openrouter.*` — not a bundle-owned config tree.\n\nIf a stable `symfony/ai-bundle` ships later, the migration path is:\n\n1. Replace `parameters:` block with `ai:` config tree\n2. Swap manual HTTP Client calls for bundle-injected AI service\n3. Remove custom service wiring\n\nUntil then, the `ai.yaml` comment block documents this as a deliberate architectural deviation.",
