            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/.opencode/skills/triageflow/SKILL.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # TriageFlow Skill\n2: \n3: > Domain-specific conventions for TriageFlow: AI-assisted patient triage showcase. Load this skill before working on any medical/AI domain logic, data modeling, or triage pipeline code.\n4: \n5: ## When to Load This Skill\n6: \n7: Load before:\n8: - Creating or modifying triage pipeline logic\n9: - Working with AI integration (symfony/ai)\n10: - Designing medical domain models\n11: - Building patient intake UI\n12: - Generating synthetic medical data\n13: - Writing system prompts for AI triage analysis\n14: \n15: ## Medical Domain Conventions\n16: \n17: ### Clinical Terminology\n18: \n19: | Term | Type | Values |\n20: |------|------|--------|\n21: | **Urgency Level** | Enum | `LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `EMERGENCY` |\n22: | **Specialist Type** | Enum | `GP`, `CARDIOLOGIST`, `DERMATOLOGIST`, `NEUROLOGIST`, `ORTHOPEDIST`, `GASTROENTEROLOGIST`, `PULMONOLOGIST`, `PSYCHIATRIST` |\n23: | **Symptom** | Value Object | String with validation (3-100 chars, alphanumeric + spaces) |\n24: | **Triage Status** | Enum | `pending`, `processing`, `completed`, `failed` |\n25: \n26: ### Synthetic Data Rules\n27: \n28: 1. **All patient data is SYNTHETIC** — generated by AI, tagged with `isSynthetic: true`\n29: 2. **Never use real medical records** — even as test fixtures\n30: 3. **Synthetic patients have fake demographics** — ages 18-85, randomized genders\n31: 4. **Symptoms span all specialist types** — AI varies domains for rich demo data\n32: 5. **Urgency distribution varies** — realistic spread (not all EMERGENCY)\n33: \n34: ### AI Prompt Engineering\n35: \n36: **System Prompt Template (Triage Analysis):**\n37: ```\n38: You are a medical triage assistant for a DEMONSTRATION system.\n39: \n40: Analyze the patient's reported symptoms and context to provide:\n41: 1. The most appropriate medical specialist\n42: 2. An urgency level based on symptom severity\n43: 3. A brief medical justification (2-3 sentences)\n44: \n45: Available specialists: GP, CARDIOLOGIST, DERMATOLOGIST, NEUROLOGIST,\n46:   ORTHOPEDIST, GASTROENTEROLOGIST, PULMONOLOGIST, PSYCHIATRIST\n47: \n48: Urgency levels:\n49:   - LOW: Non-urgent, routine care appropriate within weeks\n50:   - MEDIUM: Should see specialist within days\n51:   - HIGH: Requires prompt attention within 24 hours\n52:   - EMERGENCY: Immediate medical attention required\n53: \n54: CRITICAL RULES:\n55: - This is a DEMONSTRATION. Never provide actual medical advice.\n56: - Respond ONLY with valid JSON matching the schema.\n57: - All analysis is synthetic — do not reference real medical guidelines.\n58: - If symptoms are ambiguous, default to GP with MEDIUM urgency.\n59: ```\n60: \n61: **System Prompt Template (Synthetic Case Generator):**\n62: ```\n63: You are a synthetic medical data generator for a DEMONSTRATION system.\n64: \n65: Generate a realistic but FICTIONAL patient case with:\n66: 1. Patient age (18-85)\n67: 2. Patient gender\n68: 3. A set of 2-4 related symptoms (from various medical domains)\n69: 4. A plausible medical context (no real patient data)\n70: \n71: Vary the medical domains across calls: cardiology, dermatology,\n72: neurology, orthopedics, gastroenterology, pulmonology, psychiatry.\n73: \n74: CRITICAL: All data is SYNTHETIC. Do not use real patient records.\n75: Respond with valid JSON: {\"age\": int, \"gender\": \"male\"|\"female\", \"symptoms\": [...], \"context\": \"...\"}\n76: ```\n77: \n78: ### Output Parsing Rules\n79: \n80: ```php\n81: // Always validate AI output against expected schema\n82: $validSpecialists = SpecialistType::cases();\n83: $validUrgencies = UrgencyLevel::cases();\n84: \n85: if (!in_array($result['specialist'], array_column($validSpecialists, 'value'))) {\n86:     throw new InvalidAiResponseException(\"Unknown specialist: {$result['specialist']}\");\n87: }\n88: \n89: if (!in_array($result['urgency'], array_column($validUrgencies, 'value'))) {\n90:     throw new InvalidAiResponseException(\"Unknown urgency: {$result['urgency']}\");\n91: }\n92: ```\n93: \n94: ## Architecture Constraints\n95: \n96: 1. **AI calls are ALWAYS async** — dispatched through Symfony Messenger\n97: 2. **Triage pipeline is a CQRS flow** — SubmitTriageCommand → Handler → AI analysis → TriageCompletedEvent\n98: 3. **Frontend polls for results** — TanStack Query `refetchInterval` while status is `processing`\n99: 4. **Synthetic cases are scheduled** — Symfony Scheduler, every 60 seconds, can be disabled via env\n100: 5. **Admin overrides are allowed** — admin can manually change triage result (for demo purposes)\n101: \n102: ## Testing Domain Logic\n103: \n104: ```php\n105: // Use data providers for medical scenarios\n106: #[DataProvider('triageScenarioProvider')]\n107: public function testTriageScenarios(\n108:     array $symptoms,\n109:     string $expectedSpecialist,\n110:     string $expectedUrgency,\n111: ): void {\n112:     // Mock AI to return expected values\n113:     // Verify domain logic correctly processes AI output\n114: }\n115: \n116: public static function triageScenarioProvider(): array\n117: {\n118:     return [\n119:         'chest pain + shortness of breath' => [\n120:             ['chest pain', 'shortness of breath'],\n121:             'CARDIOLOGIST',\n122:             'HIGH',\n123:         ],\n124:         'mild skin rash' => [\n125:             ['skin rash', 'mild itching'],\n126:             'DERMATOLOGIST',\n127:             'LOW',\n128:         ],\n129:     ];\n130: }\n131: ```\n132: \n133: ## Do's and Don'ts\n134: \n135: ### ✅ Do\n136: - Tag ALL data as synthetic (`isSynthetic: true`)\n137: - Validate AI output against enums before storing\n138: - Use async processing for AI calls\n139: - Provide fallback on AI failure (default to `GP / MEDIUM`)\n140: - Log AI raw responses for debugging (`aiRawResponse` field)\n141: - Use `deepseek-reasoner` for complex cases, `deepseek-chat` for standard\n142: \n143: ### ❌ Don't\n144: - Store real patient data — ever\n145: - Make blocking AI calls in HTTP request lifecycle\n146: - Skip validation of AI output\n147: - Hard-code medical knowledge in code (goes in system prompt)\n148: - Use real medical guidelines in prompts\n149: - Expose raw AI responses to frontend without transformation\n150: \n151: ## Related Documentation\n152: \n153: - `../../agents.md` — Master project configuration\n154: - `../../backend/agents.md` — Backend implementation rules\n155: - `../../frontend/agents.md` — Frontend implementation rules\n156: - https://github.com/symfony/ai — symfony/ai package docs\n157: - https://symfony.com/doc/current/scheduler.html — Scheduler component\n158: - https://symfony.com/doc/current/messenger.html — Messenger component\n\n(End of file - total 158 lines)\n</content>",
