\"question\",\"content\":\"Your follow-up question here\"}\n48: \n49: 2. To provide a final triage result:\n50: {\"type\":\"result\",\"specialist\":\"GENERAL_PRACTITIONER\",\"urgency\":\"MEDIUM\",\"justification\":\"Brief medical justification.\"}\n51: \n52: Character limit rules:\n53: - User initial descriptions are limited to 500 characters\n54: - User answers to questions are limited to 300 characters\n55: - Your responses must be concise, under 1000 characters\n56: \n57: If you have enough information to determine a specialist and urgency, provide a\n58: result. Otherwise, ask a single focused follow-up question to gather the most\n59: critical missing information.\n60: PROMPT;\n61:     }\n62: \n63:     /**\n64:      * Builds the full conversation context as an array of messages suitable\n65:      * for the OpenRouter chat completion API.\n66:      *\n67:      * The returned array follows the OpenAI-compatible format:\n68:      *   [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"...\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"...\"}, ...]\n69:      *\n70:      * Message ordering:\n71:      *   1. System prompt (role: system)\n72:      *   2. Conversation history entries, mapped by type (in chronological order)\n73:      *   3. Current user message (role: user)\n74:      *\n75:      * History entry type-to-role mapping:\n76:      *   - initial_description → user (patient's opening complaint)\n77:      *   - answer              → user (patient's answer to an AI question)\n78:      *   - question            → assistant (AI's follow-up question)\n79:      *   - result              → assistant (AI's final triage result)\n80:      *\n81:      * @param string $userMessage The current user message to include as the final entry\n82:      * @param array<int, array{type: string, content: string, timestamp: string}> $history\n83:      *        The conversation history entries, each with type, content, and timestamp\n84:      *\n85:      * @return array<int, array{role: string, content: string}>\n86:      *         The complete messages array for the AI model\n87:      *\n88:      * @throws \\InvalidArgumentException if a history entry has an unrecognized type\n89:      */\n90:     public function buildConversationContext(string $userMessage, array $history): array\n91:     {\n92:         $messages = [];\n93: \n94:         // 1. System prompt — sets the AI's behavior and constraints\n95:         $messages[] = [\n96:             'role' => 'system',\n97:             'content' => $this->getSystemMessage(),\n98:         ];\n99: \n100:         // 2. Map each conversation history entry to its OpenAI role\n101:         foreach ($history as $entry) {\n102:             $messages[] = [\n103:                 'role' => self::mapHistoryTypeToRole($entry['type']),\n104:                 'content' => $entry['content'],\n105:             ];\n106:         }\n107: \n108:         // 3. Current user message — always the last entry\n109:         $messages[] = [\n110:             'role' => 'user',\n111:             'content' => $userMessage,\n112:         ];\n113: \n114:         return $messages;\n115:     }\n116: \n117:     /**\n118:      * Maps a conversation history entry 'type' value to an OpenAI message 'role'.\n119:      *\n120:      * @throws \\InvalidArgumentException when the type is not one of the recognized values\n121:      */\n122:     private static function mapHistoryTypeToRole(string $type): string\n123:     {\n124:         return match ($type) {\n125:             'initial_description', 'answer' => 'user',\n126:             'question', 'result' => 'assistant',\n127:             default => throw new \\InvalidArgumentException(\n128:                 sprintf('Unknown conversation history entry type: \"%s\".', $type),\n129:             ),\n130:         };\n131:     }\n132: }\n\n(End of file - total 132 lines)\n</content>",
