              "prompt": "Execute subtask from `.tmp/tasks/issue3-triage/subtask_07.json`.\n\nAlso read `.tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue3-triage/context.md` for the full design decisions.\n\n## Key Interfaces You Depend On\n\n### OpenRouterClient (`backend/src/Shared/Infrastructure/Ai/OpenRouterClient.php`)\n```php\nfinal readonly class OpenRouterClient {\n    public function chat(array $messages, ?string $model = null): string;\n}\n```\n- `$messages` is `array<int, array{role: string, content: string}>`\n- Returns raw string content from the AI (the JSON text)\n- Throws `OpenRouterException` on retry exhaustion (3 attempts on network failure)\n\n### TriageSystemPrompt (`backend/src/Triage/Application/Service/TriageSystemPrompt.php`)\n```php\nfinal readonly class TriageSystemPrompt {\n    public function getSystemMessage(): string;\n    public function buildConversationContext(string $userMessage, array $history): array;\n}\n```\n- `buildConversationContext()` returns messages in OpenAI format with system prompt + history + current message\n- History entries: `array{type: string, content: string, timestamp: string}` \n- Types: `initial_description`, `question`, `answer`, `result`\n\n### TriageOutcome (`backend/src/Triage/Domain/Entity/TriageOutcome.php`)\n```php\nfinal readonly class TriageOutcome {\n    public static function fromAiResult(array $data): self;\n    // $data must contain: specialist, urgency, justification\n}\n```\n\n## Implementation Requirements\n\n**Class**: `App\\Triage\\Application\\Service\\TriageAnalyzer`\n**Exception**: `App\\Triage\\Application\\Service\\TriageAnalysisFailedException`\n\n### Methods\n\n**`analyzeInitial(string $description): array`**\n1. Build conversation context via `TriageSystemPrompt::buildConversationContext($description, [])`\n2. Call `OpenRouterClient::chat($messages)`\n3. Parse the returned JSON string\n4. Return parsed array:\n   - If `type=question`: `['type' => 'question', 'content' => '...']`\n   - If `type=result`: `['type' => 'result', 'specialist' => '...', 'urgency' => '...', 'justification' => '...']`\n\n**`analyzeFollowUp(string $answer, array $conversationHistory, int $currentTurn): array`**\n1. Build context with full conversation history\n2. If `$currentTurn >= 3`: append a force-result message to the conversation instructing the AI to produce a final result NOW (no more questions): `\"You have been given 3 turns to gather information. Now you MUST provide a final triage result with the specialist, urgency, and justification. Do NOT ask any more questions. Respond ONLY with the result JSON format: {\\\"type\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"specialist\\\":\\\"SPECIALIST\\\",\\\"urgency\\\":\\\"URGENCY\\\",\\\"justification\\\":\\\"Justification text.\\\"}\"`\n3. Call AI, parse JSON response\n\n### JSON Discrimination & Error Handling\n\n1. **Valid question JSON**: `{\"type\":\"question\",\"content\":\"...\"}` → return question array\n2. **Valid result JSON**: `{\"type\":\"result\",\"specialist\":\"...\",\"urgency\":\"...\",\"justification\":\"...\"}` → return result array\n3. **Malformed JSON on turns 0-2**: Treat as a question. Return: `['type' => 'question', 'content' => $rawResponse]` (wrap raw AI text)\n4. **Malformed JSON on turn >= 3**: Throw `TriageAnalysisFailedException`\n5. **`type=result` missing required keys**: Throw `TriageAnalysisFailedException`\n6. **`type=result` but turn force produces a question**: Throw `TriageAnalysisFailedException` (non-compliance at turn 3)\n7. **AI returns unknown `type` (not question/result)**: Treat same as malformed JSON\n8. **OpenRouterException from client**: Throw `TriageAnalysisFailedException`\n9. **IMPORTANT**: Do NOT validate specialist/urgency against enums — there are no enums for these in the codebase. The TriageSystemPrompt defines the valid list for the AI, but the code should accept any string value. The TriageOutcome also accepts any string.\n\n### Force-result message at turn 3\n\nAppend this as an additional `user` role message before the current user answer:\n```\n\"You have been given 3 turns to gather information. Now you MUST provide a final triage result with the specialist, urgency, and justification. Do NOT ask any more questions. Respond ONLY with the result JSON format.\"\n```\nThen the actual user answer follows. If the AI STILL returns a question → throw TriageAnalysisFailedException.\n\n### TriageAnalyzer constructor\n```php\npublic function __construct(\n    private OpenRouterClient $client,\n    private TriageSystemPrompt $prompt,\n) {}\n```\n\n## Testing (TDD — tests first!)\n\nAll tests use mocked `OpenRouterClient`. Mock `chat()` to return controlled JSON strings.\n\n**Test cases:**\n1. `analyzeInitial` returns valid question\n2. `analyzeInitial` returns valid result (AI has enough info immediately)\n3. `analyzeFollowUp` returns valid question\n4. `analyzeFollowUp` returns valid result\n5. `analyzeFollowUp` at turn 3 forces result even if AI returns question (mock returns question → verify exception)\n6. `analyzeFollowUp` at turn 3 accepts valid result (mock returns result → verify success)\n7. Malformed JSON on turn 0 (analyzeInitial) → treated as question\n8. Malformed JSON on turn 1 → treated as question\n9. Malformed JSON on turn 3 → throws TriageAnalysisFailedException\n10. Unknown type in JSON → treated as malformed\n11. Result missing required keys → throws TriageAnalysisFailedException\n12. OpenRouterException propagation → throws TriageAnalysisFailedException\n13. Class structure: final, readonly, declare(strict_types=1)\n\n## Files to Create\n- `backend/src/Triage/Application/Service/TriageAnalyzer.php`\n- `backend/src/Triage/Application/Service/TriageAnalysisFailedException.php`\n- `backend/tests/Triage/Application/Service/TriageAnalyzerTest.php`\n\n**TDD: Tests first (RED), then implementation (GREEN), then refactor.**\n\nReturn when complete with file list, test results, and any issues.",
