quest()`.\n\nBut wait — the OpenRouterClient passes `'json' => [...]` as an option to `$this->httpClient->request()`. So `$options['json']` should exist in the callback.\n\nHmm, unless the MockHttpClient callback signature is different. Let me check the error again:\n- Line 101 has `$json['model']` and the warning is \"Undefined array key 'model'\" — this would only happen if $json is `[]` (from the `??` operator).\n\nActually... maybe the issue is that the callable uses `use ($responseBody, $messages)` and there's a closure variable scoping issue. No, that shouldn't matter.\n\nLet me just try a different approach: instead of accessing `$options['json']`, access `$options['body']` (the JSON string) or check if the json key is actually set:\n\n```php\n$bodyJson = json_decode($options['body'] ?? '[]', true);\n$this->assertSame(self::DEFAULT_MODEL, $bodyJson['model']);\n```\n\nOr alternatively, just debug what keys are in `$options`.\n\nActually, I think the real bug is that MockHttpClient's callback behavior changed in Symfony 7.x. Let me just fix the tests to use `body` instead of `json`, or use `array_key_first` to check.\n\nActually, the simplest fix: change the test callbacks to use `$options['body']` and decode it, OR access `$options['json']` with proper checks. Let me just look at what Symfony documentation says about MockHttpClient callbacks.\n\nYou know what, let me just fix all three issues at once:\n\n1. Interface extraction for Category 1\n2. Fix OpenRouterClient's chat() to not retry HTTP errors\n3. Fix the test callbacks to properly read the body\n\nFor #2, I'll change the catch to `\\Throwable` and re-throw non-TransportException immediately.\nFor #3, I'll change the test to use `json_decode($options['body'] ?? '[]', true)` instead of `$options['json']`.\n\nLet me also check the \"60.0 !== 60\" issue:\nLine 301: `$this->assertSame(self::TIMEOUT, $options['timeout'] ?? null);`\n`self::TIMEOUT` is `60` (int), but `$options['timeout']` is `60` (float becau