ists and is empty `[]`, then `$json = $options['json'] ?? []` would be `[]`, and accessing `$json['model']` would trigger the warning.\n\nBut why would `$options['json']` be empty? Unless the HttpClient somehow resets it. Let me look at the MockHttpClient::request() method...\n\nActually, I bet the issue is that the MockHttpClient uses the CurlHttpClient or NativeHttpClient trait under the hood, and those traits might serialize `json` to `body` early.\n\nYou know what, let me just use a completely different approach for the test. Instead of inspecting `$options`, I'll inspect the `MockResponse` that gets returned with a callback. But actually the simpler fix: just change `$options['json']` to check `$options['body']` and decode:\n\n```php\n$body = json_decode($options['body'] ?? '', true);\n$this->assertSame(self::DEFAULT_MODEL, $body['model']);\n```\n\nThis should work regardless of whether the HttpClient passes `json` or `body`.\n\nLet me now do all the fixes in one go.\n\nFixes:\n\n1. **OpenRouterClient.php** — Change `catch (TransportExceptionInterface $e)` to `catch (\\Throwable $e)` with early re-throw for non-transport errors.\n\n2. **OpenRouterClientTest.php** — Four fixes:\n   - `testChatSendsCorrectBodyWithDefaultModel` (line 99): `$options['json'] ?? []` → `json_decode($options['body'] ?? '', true)`\n   - `testChatUsesProvidedModelWhenSpecified` (line 122): Same fix\n   - `testChatRetriesOnlyOnTransportExceptionNotHttpErrors` (lines 234-258): Expect `OpenRouterException`, verify 1 call\n   - `testChatIncludesTimeoutInRequest` (line 301): `assertSame(self::TIMEOUT, ...)` → `assertSame(self::TIMEOUT, ...)` — actually the fix is to make `self::TIMEOUT` be `60.0` or change `assertSame` to `assertEquals`. Let me use `assertEquals` for the timeout comparison.\n\n3. **OpenRouterClientInterface.php** — New file\n\n4. **OpenRouterClient.php** — Add `implements OpenRouterClientInterface`\n\n5. **TriageAnalyzer.php** — Change constructor typehint\n\n6. **TriageAnalyzerTest.php** — Change `createMock(OpenRouterClient::class)` to `createMock(OpenRouterClientInterface::class)` and update import\n\nLet me implement all of these now.",
