              "description": "Task 08: SubmitTriage Cmd/Handler",
              "prompt": "Execute subtask from `.tmp/tasks/issue3-triage/subtask_08.json`.\n\nAlso read `.tmp/sessions/2026-05-29-issue3-triage/context.md` for design decisions.\n\n## Key Dependencies\n\n### TriageSubmission entity (`backend/src/Triage/Domain/Entity/TriageSubmission.php`)\n- `TriageSubmission::submit(User $user, string $initialDescription): self` — named constructor, sets status=pending\n- `addAiQuestion(string $content): void` — status→awaiting_answer, increments currentTurn, adds 'question' entry\n- `completeWithOutcome(TriageOutcome $outcome): void` — status→completed, sets processedAt, adds 'result' entry\n- `markFailed(): void` — status→failed\n- `getConversationHistory()`: returns `array<int, array{type: string, content: string, timestamp: string}>`\n\n### TriageAnalyzer (`backend/src/Triage/Application/Service/TriageAnalyzer.php`)\n- `analyzeInitial(string $description): array` — returns `['type' => 'question', 'content' => '...']` or `['type' => 'result', 'specialist' => '...', 'urgency' => '...', 'justification' => '...']`\n- Throws `TriageAnalysisFailedException` on failure\n\n### TriageSubmissionRepository interface (`backend/src/Triage/Domain/Repository/TriageSubmissionRepository.php`)\n- `save(TriageSubmission $submission): void`\n- `findById(Uuid $id): ?TriageSubmission`\n\n### TriageOutcome\n- `TriageOutcome::create(string $specialist, string $urgency, string $justification): self`\n\n## Design Flow for SubmitTriageHandler\n\nThe Handler creates a new submission AND runs the initial AI analysis synchronously (user is waiting for the first question). The flow:\n\n1. Validate initial description length (max 500 chars) — throw `\\InvalidArgumentException`\n2. Create `TriageSubmission::submit($command->user, $command->initialDescription)` → status = Pending\n3. Persist via repository\n4. Call `TriageAnalyzer::analyzeInitial($command->initialDescription)`\n5. Based on analyzer return:\n   - **Result** (`type=result`): Create TriageOutcome via `TriageOutcome::create(...)`, call `$submission->completeWithOutcome($outcome)`, persist\n   - **Question** (`type=question`): Call `$submission->addAiQuestion($content)`, persist. Optionally dispatch `ProcessTriageMessage` for async processing of subsequent answers (inject `MessageBusInterface` if dispatching)\n6. On `TriageAnalysisFailedException`: call `$submission->markFailed()`, persist\n7. Return the submission\n\nNote: Use `EntityManagerInterface` for flushing after all changes.\n\n## Files to Create\n- `backend/src/Triage/Application/Command/SubmitTriageCommand.php`\n- `backend/src/Triage/Application/Command/SubmitTriageHandler.php`\n- `backend/tests/Triage/Application/Command/SubmitTriageHandlerTest.php`\n\n## Testing (TDD — tests first!)\nAll tests mock TriageSubmissionRepository, TriageAnalyzer, and EntityManagerInterface. Use real TriageSubmission entities.\n\nTest cases:\n1. Handler creates submission, persists it, calls analyzer, returns question → submission has question in conversation\n2. Handler returns result → submission completed, outcome set, processedAt set\n3. Description exceeds 500 chars → throws InvalidArgumentException\n4. Analyzer throws → submission status = failed\n5. Handler persists entity before calling analyzer (test via spy)\n\n**TDD: Tests first (RED), then implementation (GREEN), then refactor.**\n\nReturn when complete with file list, test results, and any issues.",
