        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "## Status Report\n\n### Completed\n| Batch | Tasks | Tests |\n|-------|-------|-------|\n| 1: Foundation | 01-04 | 61/61 ✅ |\n| 2: AI Layer | 05-07 | 53/53 ✅ |\n| 3: Pipeline | 08-09 (code written) | ❌ can't run |\n\n### Current Blocker\n\n**`services.yaml` references `%ai.openrouter.*%` parameters that don't resolve** — the `config/packages/ai.yaml` `parameters:` block isn't being loaded by Symfony's container compiler. This breaks ALL container-dependent tests (16 tests: repository tests, auth tests).\n\n**Impact**: Django repository tests, auth tests, and any test using `KernelTestCase` fail. The 16 errors are all `\"non-existent parameter ai.openrouter.base_url\"`.\n\n### What Caused It\n\nTask 05's `services.yaml` change added explicit parameter wiring for `OpenRouterClient` using `%ai.openrouter.*%`. These parameters are defined in `config/packages/ai.yaml`, but the container compiler fails to load them — likely because `services.yaml` is processed first and the parameter resolution fails at compile time.\n\n### Proposed Fix\n\nMove the AI parameters directly into `services.yaml` (remove the separate `ai.yaml` reference) — define them as inline `parameters:` values with env defaults. Or: remove the explicit `OpenRouterClient` service definition entirely, letting autowiring handle it with `#[Autowire]` attributes on the class.\n\nThe simpler fix: define the parameters directly in `services.yaml`'s `parameters:` section alongside the service binding.\n\n### Remaining Work\n- Fix the parameter loading issue (blocker)\n- Fix 5 test failures (file path warnings in `file_get_contents` for strict_types checks)\n- Then: Messenger routing already configured ✅ (Task 10)\n- Then: Batch 4 (Controllers) + Batch 5 (Frontend)\n\n**Approval requested to apply the fix (move AI params into services.yaml).**\n\n\n\n",
