          "type": "text",
          "text": "## ✅ Issue #3 — Triage Interview: Complete\n\n### Final Results\n\n| Layer | Verdict | Details |\n|-------|---------|---------|\n| **Backend** | ✅ | 170 tests, 513 assertions — all green |\n| **TypeScript** | ✅ | `tsc -b` — clean |\n| **ESLint** | ✅ | Zero errors, zero warnings |\n| **Vitest** | ✅ | 4 files, 41 tests — all green |\n\n### What Was Built\n\n**Backend** (15 files + migration):\n- `TriageStatus` enum (5-state) + `TriageOutcome` Doctrine Embeddable\n- `TriageSubmission` entity (conversation history, turn counting, character limits)\n- Repository (interface + Doctrine impl) + migration\n- AI: `OpenRouterClient` (+ interface), `TriageSystemPrompt`, `TriageAnalyzer` (+ interface)\n- Pipeline: `SubmitTriageCommand`/Handler, `ProcessTriageMessage`/Handler, Messenger routing\n- `TriageController`: 5 endpoints (submit/answer/status/result/submissions) with ownership checks\n- `TestTriageAnalyzer`: static test double for functional tests\n\n**Frontend** (12 files):\n- `useTriagePolling`: TanStack Query polling hook\n- `useTriageInterview`: 6-state interview state machine\n- `TriagePage`: initial symptom → conversation → answer input → result redirect\n- `TriageResultPage`: outcome card + urgency badge + full conversation history\n- Components: `ConversationBubble`, `SymptomInput`, `AnswerInput`, `UrgencyBadge`, `OutcomeCard`\n- Updated TypeScript types (status machine, TriageOutcome, dropped `role`)\n\n**Total: 211 tests, 554 assertions** across full stack.\n\nThe Triage Interview is fully functional — users can submit symptoms, receive AI follow-up questions via polling, answer them, and get a triage recommendation with urgency and specialist.",
