st code, `willReturnQuestionOnNextCall()` should configure the analyzer to return a question. Let me check if the test is using the right config.\n\nActually, looking at the test flow:\n1. TestTriageAnalyzer::willReturnQuestionOnNextCall() — sets up\n2. POST /api/triage/submit → handler calls analyzeInitial → gets question → status = awaiting_answer\n3. GET /api/triage/result/{id} → gets submission → getOutcome() returns null\n\nBut the test output shows outcome has null fields. This means getOutcome() returns a non-null TriageOutcome object with null fields. But TriageOutcome's constructor requires non-null strings, so this shouldn't be possible...\n\nWait — I made the TriageOutcome fields `?string = null` earlier to fix the Doctrine embeddable issue. When Doctrine hydrates a submission where all outcome columns are null, it creates a TriageOutcome with null fields. Even though the entity has `private ?TriageOutcome $outcome = null`, Doctrine might still hydrate the embeddable with null fields.\n\nThe fix: at the controller level, check for complete outcome (all three fields non-null) rather than just non-null outcome object. Or better: check `$submission->getStatus() === TriageStatus::Completed`.",
