`POST /api/register`, onSuccess navigate to `/login` with `{ registered: true }`, minLength={8}. Dark mode. Two eslint fixes: `void` on navigate promise, `unknown` instead of `any` on mutation error handler.\n132: \n133: ### Fixes During Implementation\n134: \n135: - **symfony/uid** — missing from Issue #1; installed for UUID generation\n136: - **symfony/validator** — missing; installed for RegistrationController validation\n137: - **symfony/browser-kit** — missing; installed for WebTestCase/KernelBrowser\n138: - **composer.json cleanup** — removed uninstallable packages (`symfony/maker-bundle ^2.0`, `symfony/profiler-pack`) that blocked composer install\n139: - **DAMA bundle** — plan referenced it but was never installed; removed from bundles.php, tests use direct DB (no transaction isolation)\n140: - **UUID generator** — `doctrine.uuid_generator` throws `UuidFactory` class-not-found; switched to manual `Uuid::v4()` in constructor\n141: - **Test DB isolation** — no DAMA = no transactional rollback; fixed with `uniqid()` emails to prevent cross-test contamination\n142: - **JWT private key permissions** (`c46f04b`) — `private.pem` was 0600 owned by host user; PHP-FPM runs as `www-data` inside Docker so login returned 500 \"Signature key does not exist or is not readable\". Fixed with `chmod 644` + Dockerfile RUN command.\n143: \n144: ### Push Status\n145: \n146: | Repo | Remote | Head |\n147: |------|--------|------|\n148: | Backend | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | `bb8f4a3` |\n149: | Frontend | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | `9c09721` |\n150: | Docs | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | up-to-date |\n151: \n152: ### Commits\n153: \n154: | Repo | Commit | Message |\n155: |------|--------|---------|\n156: | Backend | `8f63861` | test: add PHPUnit test infrastructure |\n157: | Backend | `144fea2` | feat: add User entity with tests, repository, and migration |\n158: | Backend | `d007c67` | feat: add JWT authentication with login endpoint and role enrichment |\n159: | Backend | `b